hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","1824 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, that Aws ibn al-Samit performed zihar from his wife Khawlah bint Tha'labah, and she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. Aws suffered from a mental disorder, and the Qur'an was revealed: Those who perform zihar from their women then return to what they said, then freeing a slave before they touch one another. He said to his wife: Tell him to free a slave. She said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who gave you what He gave you, I came only out of mercy for him. Then the Qur'an was revealed while she was with him in the house, and he said: Tell him to fast two consecutive months. She said: By the One who gave you what He gave you, he cannot do it. He said: Tell him to give charity to sixty poor persons. She said: O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing with which to give charity. He said: Then go to so-and-so the Ansari, for he has half a wasq of dates; he told me he wants to give it in charity, so let him take it and give it in charity to sixty poor persons."
"3002","1825 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hakam ibn Aban narrating from Ikrimah, he said, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (saying) that he had performed zihar from his wife and that he had approached her before fulfilling what was upon him. He said: And what carried you to that? He said: O Prophet of Allah, I saw the whiteness of her leg in the moonlight. He said: Then keep away until you fulfill what is upon you."
"3003","1826 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, that a man performed zihar from his wife and then approached her before fulfilling, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Keep away from her until you fulfill what is upon you."
"3004","1827 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was said to Ata while I was listening: A man performs zihar from his wife and then has intercourse with her before expiating? He said: Evil is what he did. I said to Ata: Is there a prescribed punishment upon him or something fixed? He said: Let him seek Allah's forgiveness and then keep away from her until he expiates."
"3005","1828 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: If the one who performed zihar has intercourse before expiating, let him refrain from approaching her, seek forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, repent to Him, and expiate a single expiation."
"3006","1829 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: It is a sin he has committed; let him seek Allah's forgiveness and not return to her until he expiates, and upon him is a single expiation."
"3007","1830 - Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, about a man who performed zihar and then approached her before expiating, he said: Upon him are two expiations."
"3008","1831 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us: Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar said about a man who performed zihar from three wives, he said: Upon him is a single expiation."
"3009","1832 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, he said: I asked him about that, and he said: Upon him is a single expiation."
"3010","1833 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, they said: Upon him are three expiations."
"3011","Chapter on what suffices in zihar regarding the slave. 1834 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Freeing a Jew or a Christian does not suffice in zihar. And he used to say: Nothing suffices in any of the expiations except freeing a Muslim."
"3012","1835 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he said: Freeing a child does not suffice in the expiation of zihar."
"3013","1836 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he considered freeing a Jew and a Christian to be permissible in the expiation of zihar."
"3014","1837 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, the like of that."
"3015","1838 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to permit freeing a one-eyed person in the expiation of zihar, but did not permit freeing a blind person."
"3016","1839 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, that he considered freeing a mother of a child to be permissible in the expiation of zihar."
"3017","1840 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: A man informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: Freeing a mother of a child is not allowed in the expiation of zihar. And he considered freeing a mudabbara (a slave promised freedom upon her master's death) in the expiation of zihar to be permissible."
"3018","1841 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Hajjaj informed us, from Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Ibrahim, that he said: A mother of a child is not allowed in the expiation of zihar, nor is a woman freed after death (mu'taqah 'an dubur) allowed. I said: Why is a woman freed after death not allowed to be freed (for it)? He said: Because of what is disputed about her."
"3019","1842 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: One who heard al-Hakam informed me, saying: A mother of a child and a woman freed after death do not suffice in the expiation of zihar, because manumission has already taken effect in both. Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym said: And it is the (adopted) opinion."
"3020","1843 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, that a man among his companions said to his wife: If I approach you for a year, then you are to me like my mother's back. So we went to al-Sha'bi and asked him, and he said: Ila' does not enter into zihar, nor does zihar enter into ila'."
"3021","1844 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If a man performs zihar from his wife and then he dies, or she dies, before he expiates, he said: They inherit from one another."
"3022","1845 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man who performs zihar from his wife and then approaches her before expiating, he said: Let him seek forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and not return, and upon him is a single expiation."
"3023","1846 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and al-Hasan, and from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, they said: There is no time limit for the one who performed zihar; when he expiates, she is his wife."
"3024","Chapter on what has come regarding the zihar of women. 1847 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, about a woman who performs zihar from her husband, he said: It is nothing; zihar belongs only to men."
"3025","1848 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that A'ishah bint Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah said: If I marry Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr, then he is to me like my father's back. She married him and asked about that, and she was ordered to expiate, so she freed a slave boy of hers worth two thousand."
"3026","1849 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, the like of that."
"3027","1850 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, he said: Ibrahim used to say: If she says it after the man has married, then it is nothing."
"3028","1851 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man sat with us and we asked his lineage, and he said: I am the one whom A'ishah bint Talhah freed on account of her statement about Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr."
"3029","1852 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: If he performs zihar from his wife (likening her to) one with whom marriage is forbidden (dhi mahram), then it is zihar."
"3030","Chapter on what has come regarding zihar from a slave woman. 1853 - Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: I asked Mujahid about zihar from a slave woman, and it was as if he did not consider it anything. I said: Does not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say in His Book: Those who perform zihar from their women - is she not among women? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: And bring two witnesses from among your men - are slaves not among men? Is the testimony of slaves then allowed?"
"3031","1854 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say about zihar from a slave woman: Like zihar from a free woman."
"3032","1855 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If he had had intercourse with her and then performs zihar from her, then it is zihar, and if he had not had intercourse with her, then there is no zihar upon him."
"3033","1856 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked about a man who performs zihar from his slave woman, he said: He is not to approach her until he expiates the expiation of zihar. I said: May he free her for the expiation? He said: Yes. I said: If he wants to marry her afterwards? He said: Let him do so if he wishes."
"3034","1857 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Zihar is from every female with whom marriage is forbidden (dhat mahram)."
"3035","1858 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from one of his companions, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: Zihar is from every female with whom marriage is forbidden."
"3036","Chapter on the expiation of the slave in zihar. 1859 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, that they said about a slave when he performs zihar from his wife: He fasts two consecutive months."
"3037","1860 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he says: If his master permits him to free, then let him free, and if he does not permit him, then let him fast two consecutive months."
"3038","1861 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Tawus: What did your father say about the zihar of the slave? He said: He used to say: Upon him is the like of the expiation of the free man."
"3039","1862 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, he said: Zihar from a slave woman is like zihar from a free woman, and in it is the expiation."
"3040","Chapter on what has come regarding a man who embraces Islam while having more than four wives, or two sisters. 1863 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardhal, from al-Harith ibn Qays al-Asadi, he said: I embraced Islam while having eight wives, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to choose four of them."
"3041","1864 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from one of the children of al-Harith ibn Qays ibn Umayrah al-Asadi, that al-Harith embraced Islam while having eight wives, and he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: Choose four of them."
"3042","1865 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Kalbi informed us, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardhal, from al-Harith ibn Qays, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I embraced Islam and they embraced with me; I emigrated and they emigrated with me. He said: Then choose four of them. So I would say to the one I wanted to keep: Come, and to the one I wanted to part from: Go back. She would say: I adjure you by kinship, I adjure you by the child. Al-Kalbi said: And Abu Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Harith ibn Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"3043","1866 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: He chooses four of them."
"3044","1867 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim al-Makki narrated to us, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Ibrahim, he said: He chooses the first four and parts from the latter ones."
"3045","1868 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that a man embraced Islam while having ten wives, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to choose four of them."
"3046","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, 'Awf informed us, he said: a shaykh in the gathering of elders narrated to us that a man from Bakr ibn Wa'il had combined two sisters in marriage, then he embraced Islam in the time of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, so 'Umar said to him: Choose one of them. 'Awf said: So I mentioned it to some people of Bakr ibn Wa'il and they recognized the man, and said: that is Hannam al-Bakri, a man from us, and there was harshness in him, and he used to say to the one he parted from: You are indeed my wife, but 'Umar prevailed over me concerning you."
"3047","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, and al-A'mash informed me, from Ibrahim, he said: Every oath that prevents intercourse is ila'."
"3048","Chapter: What has come concerning ila'. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say that also."
"3049","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who brought his wife to some people, and she made a zihar-like claim to them, so they made her husband swear, saying: Your wife is divorced if you have intercourse with her until she weans our boy; is it not that if he leaves her for four months she becomes separated through ila', and if he approaches her before the boy is weaned she is divorced three times? He said: Yes."
"3050","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he was heard saying that."
"3051","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abi 'Atiyyah al-Asadi, that he asked 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about having married his brother's wife while she was nursing his brother's son, and he said: She is divorced if I approach her until he weans him; so 'Ali said: You only intended good for yourself and your brother's son, so there is no ila' upon you; ila' is only what occurs in anger."
"3052","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say the like of that."
"3053","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Waki' narrated to us, from Abi Fazarah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: Ila' is only in anger."
"3054","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'qa' ibn Yazid al-Dabbi informed us, he said: I asked al-Hasan about ila', and he said: Ila' is only what occurs in anger. He said: And I asked Ibn Sirin and he said: I do not know what they say and what they bring; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: For those who swear abstention from their wives is a waiting of four months, then if they return, Allah is Forgiving, Merciful; and if they resolve upon divorce, Allah is Hearing, Knowing."
"3055","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'fur al-'Abdi narrated to me, from 'Atiyyah ibn Jubayr, from his father Jubayr, that he swore not to approach his wife for two years until she weans her child, so it was said to him: What have you done? So he came to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him, and he said to him: If you were in anger then she has become separated from you, otherwise she is your wife."
"3056","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I swore not to approach my wife for two years, so he said: I see nothing but that ila' has entered upon you. He said: I only said that because she is nursing my child. He said: Then there is none."
"3057","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Yahya, freedman of Mu'adh ibn 'Afra', from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: Ila' is only that a man swears never to approach his wife."
"3058","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, that he asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about ila', he said: It is nothing."
"3059","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When a man takes an ila' oath from his wife and four months pass, it is not ila' until he divorces. So I said to him: Al-Hasan says: When four months pass it is an irrevocable divorce. He said: When you meet al-Hasan convey salam to him, and tell him that evil is what he said."
"3060","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: Ila' is not divorce, but it is disobedience, and disobedience does not impose divorce upon him; rather he is halted at four months, so either he returns or he divorces."
"3061","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Qudamah al-Harith ibn 'Ubayd al-Iyadi narrated to us, he said: 'Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The ila' of the people of Jahiliyyah was a year and two years, and more than that, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fixed four months; so whoever's ila' is less than four months, it is not ila'."
"3062","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from 'Amir al-Ahwal, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Whoever swears not to approach his wife for a month, then leaves her for four months, it is not ila'."
"3063","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd Allah, that he said concerning ila': When four months pass, it is one irrevocable divorce."
"3064","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that he used to say the like of that."
"3065","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd Allah, and Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Abd Allah, that he used to say: When a man takes an ila' oath from his wife and four months pass before he approaches her, she becomes separated from him with one divorce, and she observes 'iddah of three menstrual cycles, and he may propose to her during them if he wishes and she wishes."
"3066","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abi 'Ubaydah, from Masruq, from 'Abd Allah, that he said the like of that."
"3067","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abi Qilabah, that al-Nu'man ibn Bashir took an ila' oath from his wife, so 'Abd Allah said to him: If four months pass over you before you approach her, then acknowledge one divorce."
"3068","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-A'mash informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: When a man takes an ila' oath from his wife and the four months pass, it is an irrevocable divorce."
"3069","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar, he said: They both used to say: When a man takes an ila' oath from his wife and the four months pass before he returns, it is an irrevocable divorce."
"3070","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The resolve upon divorce is the expiry of the four months, and returning (fay') is intercourse."
"3071","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Returning (fay') is intercourse."
"3072","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"3073","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: Returning (fay') is intercourse."
"3074","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say concerning one who took an ila' oath from his wife then could not approach her due to menstruation, postnatal bleeding, or a matter in which he has an excuse: He testifies to the return, and she is his wife."
"3075","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah and Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who takes an ila' oath from his wife, then cannot have intercourse due to an excuse until four months pass: He testifies to the return, and she is his wife."
"3076","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: He returns, and returning (fay') is intercourse."
"3077","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, the like of it."
"3078","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that a man from Muharib took an ila' oath from his wife, and when the four months approached he wanted to return to her, but the woman entered postnatal bleeding, so he came to 'Alqamah and al-Aswad and they said: Testify to the return, and she is your wife."
"3079","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: A guest stayed with Abi al-Sha'tha', and he had taken an ila' oath from his wife and she entered postnatal bleeding, so he wanted to return but could not because of her bleeding, so he came to 'Alqamah and mentioned that to him, and 'Alqamah said to him: Have you not already returned in your heart and consented? He said: Yes. He said: You have returned; she is your wife."
"3080","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Salim, from 'Amir, he said: Every oath a man swears involving not approaching his wife for four months is ila'."
"3081","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus, 'Awf, and Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: Returning is testification, when he has an excuse of illness, menstruation, or postnatal bleeding."
"3082","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Returning (fay') is intercourse."
"3083","Chapter: Who said the one taking ila' is halted at four months. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Amr ibn Salamah, he said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When a man takes an ila' oath from his wife, he is halted until he returns or divorces."
"3084","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Marwan, from 'Ali, the like of it."
"3085","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Amr ibn Salamah al-Kindi informed me that he witnessed 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, halting a man at four months, either to return or to divorce."
"3086","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I witnessed 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, halting a man at four months in al-Rahbah, either to return or to divorce."
"3087","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us from al-Shaybani, he said: Bukayr informed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of it."
"3088","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he said concerning one taking ila' from his wife: He is halted at four months, either to return or to divorce."
"3089","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from his father, that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning ila': He is halted at four months, either to return or to divorce."
"3090","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man would take ila' from his wife and remain more than four months, and 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, did not consider that ila'."
"3091","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, considered ila' nothing until halting."
"3092","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: Nineteen men from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would halt in ila'."
"3093","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam halted one taking ila' after six months."
"3094","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from some of his companions, from Qatadah, that Abu al-Darda' used to say: It is disobedience; he is halted at four months, either to return or to divorce."
"3095","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, he said: I said to my father: People claim ila' is divorce. He said: They lied; it is only something they were admonished with."
"3096","Chapter: For what an oath counts as ila'. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: He did not consider ila' except with an oath."
"3097","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: When a man says to his wife - and she has gone to her family in anger - By Allah I will not come to you until you come to me: if the four months pass, there is no ila' upon him."
"3098","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning a man angry with his wife not approaching her for four months, he said: No ila' falls upon him unless he swore, or said: I will not approach you; and whatever is from anger on the wife's part, no ila' falls in it."
"3099","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: When a man says to his wife, By Allah I will not approach her tonight, then leaves her for four months: if he left her because of his oath, it is ila'."
"3100","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, concerning one who took ila' then divorced, he said: Divorce demolishes ila'."
"3101","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Divorce demolishes ila'. And al-Sha'bi said: They race as if they are two racehorses."
"3102","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: Divorce demolishes ila', but they are like two racehorses; whichever precedes is taken by it, and if they stop together both are taken."
"3103","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say the like of al-Sha'bi's saying."
"3104","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: When he takes ila' then divorces, they are like two racehorses."
"3105","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to me that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: They race; and Ibn Mas'ud used to say: Divorce demolishes ila'. Hushaym said: The saying is upon what 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said."
"3106","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: When a man takes ila' from his wife then divorces her, if the 'iddah of divorce passes, divorce demolishes ila' and it is one divorce; and if the 'iddah of ila' passes before the 'iddah of divorce, it is two divorces."
"3107","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: The ila' of a slave from a free woman is four months, and his ila' from a slave woman is two months."
"3108","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man makes zihar from his wife while she is a slave woman, upon him is half the expiation of a free woman; and if he makes zihar from his slave woman, upon him is the expiation of a free woman."
"3109","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who said to his wife: By Allah I will not speak to you, then four months passed before he spoke to her, he said: I fear it is ila', though ila' was only in intercourse."
"3110","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Anas took an ila' oath from his wife, then left, and came after the time of ila' had passed, and entered upon his wife; a man met him and said: What did you do about your oath? He said: I did not remember it. So he came to 'Abd Allah and mentioned that to him, and he said: Go inform her that she has separated from you, then propose to her; so he proposed to her and married her for a ratl of silver."
"3111","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man came to Shurayh and said: He took an ila' oath from his wife and four months passed before he returned to her, so Shurayh said to him: And if they resolve upon divorce, Allah is Hearing, Knowing. The man said to him: Give me a fatwa. He did not add to that. So he went to Masruq and told him what had happened, and Masruq said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Umayyah; if people did like he did, who would relieve you? Then he said: When the four months pass, she separates from you with one divorce, and observes 'iddah of three menses, and you propose to her if you wish, and none but you proposes to her until the 'iddah ends."
"3112","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, with the like of Mughirah's hadith. Al-Sha'bi said: When Masruq said what he said: Go to Shurayh. So I went to Shurayh and told him Masruq's saying, and Shurayh said to me: Do you know the man? I said: Perhaps I know him. He said: Look for him for me in the mosque. So I looked, and there he was, and I said to him: Come, Shurayh calls you. So I brought him to him, and he said to him like what Masruq had said to him."
"3113","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, that a man came to Shurayh and asked him about ila', so he recited this verse to him and returned that upon him as he had asked; then the man came to Masruq and asked him and mentioned Shurayh's saying to him, so Masruq said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Umayyah; if another were brought and said like his saying, who would relieve you? Then Masruq said: When the four months pass, she separates with one divorce, and he proposes to her during the 'iddah; and when she completes the 'iddah, he proposes to her along with the suitors."
"3114","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: When a man takes ila' and the four months pass, there is no 'iddah upon her."
"3115","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Anas took an ila' oath from his wife then left, and was absent from her for six months, then came and entered upon her; it was said to him: She has separated from you. So he came to 'Abd Allah and mentioned that to him, and he said to him: Go to her and inform her that she has separated from you, then propose to her for herself. So he came to her and informed her and proposed to her for herself, and dowered her a ratl of wariq (silver)."
"3116","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: One who takes ila' is halted at four months, either to return or to divorce."
"3117","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning ila', he said: He is halted at four months."
"3118","Chapter: The slave woman sold while she has a husband. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Abd Allah used to say: The sale of a slave woman is her divorce."
"3119","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Mas'ud said: The sale of a slave woman is her divorce."
"3120","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that he said: The sale of a slave woman is her divorce."
"3121","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When a slave marries with his master's permission then he sells him, he is not separated from her; and when a man marries off his slave woman then sells her, he used to consider her sale her divorce."
"3122","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The sale of a slave woman is divorce, and the sale of a slave is not divorce."
"3123","Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: The sale of a slave woman is her divorce."
"3124","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to say concerning the sale of a slave woman: It is her divorce."
"3125","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: The flight of a slave is his divorce."
"3126","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: 'Asim al-Ahwal informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A slave girl was gifted to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he was informed she has a husband, so he bought her marital right from her husband for five hundred dirhams upon his divorcing her."
"3127","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind and 'Ubaydah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Murrah ibn Sharahil, the owner of al-Saylahayn, sent a slave girl to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him; he asked her: Do you have a husband? She said: Yes. So he returned her, and wrote to Murrah: I found your gift occupied. So Murrah bought her marital right from her husband for five hundred dirhams, and sent her to him, and he accepted her."
"3128","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq informed us, from his father, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Yasar ibn Numayr to buy him a slave girl, so he did, then sent her to him; she told him she has a husband among her people, so he refrained from her, and wrote to him to buy her marital right from her husband, so he did. Hushaym said: And it is the saying (adopted)."
"3129","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, that his father bought a slave girl from 'Asim ibn 'Adi, and was informed she has a husband, so he returned her."
"3130","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf bought a slave girl and it was mentioned she has a husband, so he sent for him and called him and said: O my son, divorce her. He said: No, by Allah I will not divorce her. So he said: Take your slave girl. And he returned her."
"3131","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to us, that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, went out to the market and saw a slave girl and she pleased him, so he bought her; he wanted to leave with her, but her owner said: O Abu Ishaq, leave her until we order her to be combed, then we send her to you. So he left her until they did that with her; when he was alone with her she said: By Allah I am not lawful to you. He said: Why? She said: I have a husband. He said: What is with him, may Allah kill him; he wanted to make me bear upon a Muslim man's wife. So he went out with her to him, repeating that saying, until he reached him in the market; the man heard, and said: O Sa'd, stop; do not say: I am one whose supplication is answered; she is only my slave girl I married her to a slave boy of mine, and if you wish I separate them I will separate. So Sa'd said: That is not to you; he is her husband, wherever he finds her he takes her by her leg. And he returned her to him."
"3132","Chapter: The mother of a child having children from her master, then he dies leaving her, then she marries and bears children from him, then some of her child from the master dies. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, that a man from Banu Hashim had a mother of a child who bore from him, and the Hashimi died, so his umm walad married a man and he entered upon her, and she bore children from him; then the Hashimi's son from her died, and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali witnessed him; when he finished burying him he said to the husband of his slave woman: You are rightly guided; this boy has died, and you have no right to claim a share that is not yours, and I order you to separate from your wife."
"3133","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning an owned slave under whom is a free woman, and he has a free brother, and his brother died leaving no heir, he said: The slave refrains from his wife until it is known whether she is pregnant or not; if she is pregnant, her child inherits his uncle. And he used to say concerning a man with a wife having a child from another, and that child of hers died, he said: The man refrains from his wife until it is known whether she is pregnant or not."
"3134","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man's wife has a child from another and he dies, he should refrain from intercourse with her until she menstruates."
"3135","Chapter: Who divorces his wife while ill, and who inherits her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed us, from his father, from his grandfather 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that he said: No woman of my wives asks me for divorce but I divorce her; and Tamadur bint al-Asbagh, the mother of Abu Salamah, had in her character some of what is therein, so she asked him for divorce while he was ill, and he said to her: When you menstruate then become pure, inform me. So she informed him, and he divorced her irrevocably, and died in that illness of his; so 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, made her inherit from him after the 'iddah ended."
"3136","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf said: No woman asks me for divorce but I divorce her; so Tamadur bint al-Asbagh became jealous and sent to him asking her divorce, and he said to the messenger: Tell her: When she menstruates let her inform me. So she menstruated and sent to him, and he said to the messenger: Tell her: When she becomes pure let her inform me. So she became pure and sent to him while he was ill, so he became angry and said also: She is divorced irrevocably, no return to her. He did not remain but a little until he died. And 'Abd al-Rahman said: I will not make Tamadur inherit anything. So they were raised to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and that was during the 'iddah, so he made her inherit from him; then they settled with her for her share, a quarter of the eighth, for eighty thousand, but they did not pay her in full."
"3137","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Shurayh concerning one who divorced his wife thrice in his illness: She inherits him, and he does not inherit her."
"3138","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Among what 'Urwah al-Bariqi brought from 'Umar to Shurayh: In the eye of a beast is a quarter of its price, fingers are equal, wounds of men and women are equal except the tooth and the clarifying wound, the best time of a man to be truthful in acknowledging his child is at his death, and when a man divorces his wife thrice, she inherits him while she is in the 'iddah."
"3139","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: Among what 'Urwah al-Bariqi brought to Shurayh from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Fingers are equal, the little finger and the thumb are equal; wounds of men and women are equal in the tooth and the clarifying wound, and otherwise upon half; in the eye of a beast is a quarter of its price; the most right state of a man to be truthful upon at his death is in his child when he acknowledges him. Mughirah said: I forgot the fifth until 'Ubaydah reminded me: When a man divorces his wife thrice, she inherits him while she is in the 'iddah."
"3140","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abi Hashim, concerning a man divorcing his wife while ill: if he dies in that illness of his, she inherits him. So Ibn Shubrumah said to him: What if the 'iddah ends, does she marry? He said: Yes. He said: If this one dies, and the first died, does she inherit two husbands? He said: No; it returns to the 'iddah. He said: She inherits him while she is in the 'iddah."
"3141","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who divorced his wife thrice in his illness, they said: She observes the 'iddah of one whose husband died and inherits him while she is in the 'iddah."
"3142","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, that they said concerning a man who divorced his wife one or two while ill, then died, they said: She begins the 'iddah of one whose husband died and inherits him."
"3143","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, concerning a man divorcing his wife thrice in his illness, he said: She inherits him while she is in the 'iddah."
"3144","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who divorced his wife thrice while ill, he said: She has inheritance if he dies while she is in the 'iddah; when her 'iddah ends, she has no inheritance. Hushaym said: And with it we take."
"3145","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A grave chapter of divorce: when a woman inherits, she observes 'iddah."
"3146","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Harith al-'Ukli, concerning a man who divorced his wife twice in his health then became ill, then divorced her the third for the 'iddah in his illness, and died in that illness of his, he said: She does not inherit him because he did not transgress."
"3147","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, and Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah, from Abi Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf divorced his wife in his illness, and died after she had become lawful; so 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, made her inherit."
"3148","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, concerning one who divorces before consummation while ill, he said: She has half the dower, no inheritance for her, and no 'iddah upon her. Hushaym said: And with it we take."
"3149","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: She has the full dower, inheritance, and upon her is the 'iddah."
"3150","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, he said: I asked him about a man divorcing his wife irrevocably while ill, he said: They do not inherit each other, she has no maintenance, unless she is pregnant, or she is divorced harmfully in his illness and he dies while she is in her 'iddah."
"3151","Chapter: What has come concerning two Christians, one of whom embraces Islam. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Saffah, from Dawud ibn Kurdus, that a woman from Banu Tamim was under a man from Banu Taghlib and she embraced Islam, so 'Umar said: Either he embraces Islam, or we take her from him. He said: Arabs will not say I embraced Islam for a woman's private part. So he took her from him."
"3152","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning a Christian under whom is a Christian woman, and she embraced Islam, he said: Separated between them; none but us owns our women; we are over people, and people are not over us; and that is because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: To make it prevail over all religion."
"3153","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Separated between them."
"3154","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: 'Umar said: She is given the choice."
"3155","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Mutarrif and 'Uthman al-Batti informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: He is more entitled to her while she has not left the abode of hijrah."
"3156","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, that they said the like of that."
"3157","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah informed us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: She remains with him because he has a covenant. Sa'id said: Evil is what he said."
"3158","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, the like of it."
"3159","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah informed us, from Hasan ibn 'Imran, from a man, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, that Hani' ibn Qabisah's wife embraced Islam before him, and he feared separation between them, so he met Abu Sufyan ibn Harb and spoke to him to speak for him to 'Umar; so Abu Sufyan said: Hunayy, gone is the time you knew us upon; by Allah, if it reached me that I have a son in Iraq who stepped upon his people slightly, nothing would prevent me claiming him except fear of 'Umar; and none is spoken to concerning Allah's due."
"3160","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih informed us, from Mujahid, concerning a Christian woman embracing Islam under a Christian: If her husband embraces Islam while she is in the 'iddah, he is more entitled to her."
"3161","Chapter: The woman divorced thrice then marrying another, then he divorces her before touching her - does she return to the first? Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Hadrami informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, that al-Rumaysa' or al-Rumayda' came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband, claiming he does not reach her; it was not long before her husband came and said: She lies; he does reach her, but she wants to return to her first husband. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not for her until she tastes his little honey."
"3162","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'A'ishah, that the wife of Rifa'ah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was with Rifa'ah and he divorced me and made my divorce final; then Ibn al-Zubayr married me, and with him is only like the fringe of a garment. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Do you want to return to Rifa'ah? No, until you taste his little honey and he tastes yours. So Khalid ibn Sa'id called out at the door: Do you not hear, O Abu Bakr, what this woman openly says before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"3163","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Ali, that he said concerning a man who divorced his wife thrice, then she married a man after him, then he divorced her before entering upon her, 'Ali said: She does not return to the first until the other approaches her."
"3164","Sa'id narrated to us, Duwayd ibn 'Ulbah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I saw 'Ali, and heard from him a hadith I heard: He was asked about a man who divorced his wife, then another man married her after him, then divorced her before entering upon her, so he brought out his forearm, on it spots, and said: No, until he shakes her."
"3165","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'A'ishah, that she said: Until he tastes her little honey and she tastes his."
"3166","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: People say until he has intercourse with her; as for me, I say: When he marries her with a valid marriage not intending tahleel for her, there is no harm in the first marrying her."
"3167","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he said: The first has no right to marry her until the last has intercourse with her."
"3168","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, concerning a man who divorced his wife thrice and attained from her everything except he did not touch her, Ibn 'Umar said: No, until he touches her. He repeated the hadith to him, and he said: No, until he touches her. He repeated the hadith to him, and he said: No, until he takes her by her leg."
"3169","Chapter: What has come concerning the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done. Sa'id informed us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I find no muhallil nor one for whom tahleel is done except I stone him."
"3170","Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Qabisah ibn Jabir, he said: 'Umar said: I find no muhallil nor one for whom tahleel is done except I stone them both."
"3171","Sa'id narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: When the intention of one of the three - the first husband, the last husband, or the woman - is that he is a muhallil, this last marriage is void, and she is not lawful to the first."
"3172","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: When one of the three intends tahleel, he has corrupted."
"3173","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say that."
"3174","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, a man narrated to us, from Ibn 'Umar, that he said: Cursed is the one who makes lawful, the one for whom it is made lawful, and the woman made lawful."
"3175","Sa'id informed us, Muhammad ibn Nashit al-Basri narrated to us, he said: I asked Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani about a man divorcing his wife irrevocably, he said: Cursed is the one who makes lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful; they were called in Jahiliyyah the borrowed billy-goat."
"3176","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, that a man from the people of Medina divorced his wife thrice, and regretted, and it reached from him what Allah willed; it was said to him: Look for a man to make her lawful for you. And in Medina was a man from the Bedouins of noble lineage, driven to Medina, needy, having nothing to cover with except two patches, a patch covering his front and a patch covering his back. So they sent to him and said to him: Will you marry a woman, enter upon her, uncover her veil, then divorce her, and we make for you a reward for that? He said: Yes. So they married him; he entered upon her, a young man of sound lineage; when he entered upon the woman and attained her, she liked him, and she said to him: Do you have good? He said: Yes, where you love; may Allah make him her ransom. She said: Look, do not divorce me for anything, for 'Umar will not force you to divorce me. In the morning he hardly opened the door before they almost broke it; when they entered upon him, they said: Divorce. He said: The matter is to so-and-so. So they said to her: Tell him to divorce you. She said: I dislike to keep having one entering upon me. So they were raised to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and told him; he said to him: If you divorce her I will do with you - and he raised his hands - and said: O Allah, You provided the one of two patches when 'Umar was stingy upon him."
"3177","Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, he said: I said to Ibrahim: Did Ibn al-Khattab make tahleel between a man and his wife? He said: No; a man had a wife of lineage and wealth, and her husband divorced her one or two, and she separated from him; then 'Umar married her and was congratulated with her, and they said: Were she not a woman without child. So 'Umar said: What is their blessing except for their children. So he divorced her before entering upon her, and her first husband married her."
"3178","Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abi Ma'shar, he said: Her first husband was al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi'ah."
"3179","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who divorced his wife thrice and she married a slave without his masters' permission and he entered upon her, he said: He is not a husband."
"3180","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: He is not a husband. Hushaym said: And it is the saying (adopted)."
"3181","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Hakam, Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hasan, concerning a woman divorced thrice by her husband, then marrying a boy not reaching puberty, and he had intercourse with her, then divorced her, he said: He is not a husband."
"3182","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah, that he said: He is a husband, and she becomes lawful to the first if he wishes. [Flag: contradicts 3181 under same chain; translated literally]"
"3183","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a slave marrying without his master's permission then divorcing her, he said: His divorce is not valid."
"3184","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: His divorce is not valid."
"3185","Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done."
"3186","Chapter: What has come concerning the impotent. Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Umar, that he used to say concerning a man when his wife enters upon him and he cannot reach her, he said: She is given a year; if he is able upon her, otherwise separated between them."
"3187","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning a man fornicating with a slave woman then buying her, he said: He used to dislike approaching her."
"3188","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that 'Umar wrote to Shurayh concerning a man when he cannot reach his wife that he gives him respite from the day she is delivered to him a year; if he reaches her, otherwise separated between them."
"3189","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, that Mu'adh Abu Halimah married the daughter of al-Nu'man ibn Harithah and could not reach her, so 'Umar gave him a year, and he could not reach her, he said: So he separated between them."
"3190","Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to me, that 'Umar, when he could not reach her, separated between them and said: Praise be to Allah who restrained him from al-Nu'man's daughter. [Flag: source syntax compressed; translated literally]"
"3191","2014 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ubaydah narrated, from Ibrahim, who used to say: 'He is granted a respite of one year from the day he is brought before the ruler; if he consummates the marriage with her, otherwise they are separated.'"
"3192","2015 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, the same as that."
"3193","2016 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, that he granted a man who could not consummate with his wife ten months."
"3194","2017 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who used to say: 'If he does not consummate with her, he is granted a term of one year and is referred to the ruler; if he consummates with her, otherwise they are separated; she receives the full dower and must observe the waiting period.'"
"3195","2018 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: 'If he consummated with her even once and is then prevented from her, no respite is granted; she remains his wife.'"
"3196","2019 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Hajjaj narrated, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that Amr ibn al-As wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning a man afflicted with a urinary ailment regarding his wife; he said: 'He is granted one year; if he succeeds, otherwise they are separated.' [Flag: opening description garbled/truncated in source]"
"3197","2020 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Hani ibn Hani, who said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, when a woman came to him and said to him: 'Will you take a woman who is neither a widow nor married?' He said: 'Then where is your husband?' She said: He is among the people. Then an old man leaning forward stood up and said: What is this woman saying? He said: Ask her whether she complains about food or clothing. Ali said: 'Nothing of that?' He said: No. He said: Nor of magic? He said: Nor of magic. He said: You are ruined and have ruined. She said: Separate me from him. He said: 'Be patient, for if Allah willed He would have tried you with worse than that.'"
"3198","2021 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent a man on some tax-collection duty, and he married a woman while he was impotent; when he returned to Umar he mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Did you inform her that you are impotent?' He said: No. He said: 'Go and inform her, then give her the choice.'"
"3199","Chapter: what has come concerning a man who cannot find maintenance for his wife. 2022 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about a man who cannot find maintenance for his wife - are they separated? He said: 'Yes.' I said: Is it a Sunnah? He said: 'A Sunnah.'"
"3200","2023 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man unable to maintain his wife; he said: 'He maintains her or they are separated.'"
"3201","2024 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'If he finds means he maintains, and if he does not find means he is not burdened beyond what he can bear.'"
"3202","2025 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said: He maintains her or divorces her."
"3203","2026 - Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: He maintains her or divorces her."
"3204","2027 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, from Ibn Shubrumah, who said: If he finds means he maintains, and if he does not find means he is not burdened with what he cannot bear."
"3205","2028 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-A'mash informed us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, that Nu'aym ibn Dajajah al-Asadi divorced his wife twice, then said to her: She is a burden (haraj) upon him; so he wrote about that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: 'Yet she is not the least of them.'"
"3206","2029 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that Nu'aym divorced his wife twice then said: She is a burden upon him; so he wrote about that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote: 'Does so-and-so think that his saying she is a burden upon him is lighter than two divorces? When this letter of mine reaches you, separate them.'"
"3207","2030 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Hasan; and Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim; and Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'When a non-Arab divorces in his own language, it is valid.'"
"3208","2031 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the same, with the addition: The divorce of every people in their own language is valid."
"3209","2032 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who says to his wife: 'Bahishtum' (you are divorced in Persian); he said: 'She is divorced.'"
"3210","Chapter: a slavegirl owned jointly by two men when one of them has intercourse with her. 2033 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated, Umayr ibn Numayr al-Hamdani informed me, who said: I heard Ibn Umar asked about a slavegirl shared between two men with whom one of them had intercourse; he said: 'He is treacherous; there is no hadd punishment upon him.'"
"3211","2034 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say: 'There is no hadd upon him, but he is lashed one hundred lashes and she is valued against him.'"
"3212","2035 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan; and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that both said: 'There is no hadd upon him, and she is valued against him if she becomes pregnant.'"
"3213","2036 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'If she becomes pregnant she is valued against him, and if she does not become pregnant he owes half her bride-price (uqr), and she remains a slavegirl as before.'"
"3214","2037 - Sa'id informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ma'bad, the in-law of al-Hakam, that a dispute was brought to Shurayh concerning two men sharing a slavegirl with whom one of them had intercourse, so he charged him half the price and half the bride-price."
"3215","Chapter: a man who owns an immoral slavegirl and makes her chaste. 2038 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning a man who commits fornication with a slavegirl then buys her: 'He used to dislike that he approach her.'"
"3216","2039 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mansur reported, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, that Ibn Mas'ud used to dislike for a man to have intercourse with his slavegirl if she had committed fornication, or to have intercourse with her while she was a polytheist."
"3217","2040 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ayyub, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, who said: They visited him at the beginning of the day while he was fasting, then visited him at its end while he had broken his fast, so they asked him and he said: 'A slavegirl passed by me and pleased me, and I add for you that she was a prostitute, so I made her chaste (by taking her).'"
"3218","2041 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: We visited Ibn Abbas in the early part of the day and found him fasting, then we went to him in the evening and found him having broken his fast, so we said to him: Were you not fasting? He said: Yes, but a slavegirl of mine came before me and pleased me, so I had intercourse with her; it was only voluntary, and I shall make up a day in its place; and I add for you that she was a prostitute, so I made her chaste, and he had practiced withdrawal from her. Sa'id said: So we learned four things in a single report."
"3219","Chapter: a man who owns a non-Muslim slavegirl - is it lawful for him to have intercourse with her. 2042 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, who said: I asked Murrah al-Hamdani about a man who has intercourse with his slavegirl while she is a Magian, and I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr; the sterner of the two in statement said: 'If they do so, they are no better than them.'"
"3220","2043 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, from Murrah al-Hamdani and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, the same."
"3221","2044 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that he said: 'When Jewish and Christian women are taken captive, they are compelled to accept Islam; if they accept Islam they are had intercourse with and employed, and if they refuse they are still had intercourse with and employed; and when Magian and idol-worshipping women are taken captive, they are compelled to accept Islam; if they accept Islam they are had intercourse with and employed, and if they do not accept Islam they are employed but not had intercourse with.'"
"3222","2045 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, that he had intercourse with a slavegirl of his after he had denied her child."
"3223","Chapter: what has come concerning slave-mothers of children. 2046 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abidah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, freed slave-mothers of children, and Umar ruled by that until he was struck, then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, took charge and ruled by that until he was struck; Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Then when I took charge I judged that they be enslaved. Abidah said: The opinion of Umar and Ali together in unity is better than the opinion of Ali alone in division."
"3224","2047 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abidah, who said: Ali addressed the people and said: Umar consulted me about slave-mothers of children, and I and Umar judged that we free them; so Umar ruled by it all his life, and Uthman all his life; then when I took charge I judged that they be enslaved. Abidah said: The opinion of Umar and Ali in unity is dearer to us than the opinion of Ali alone."
"3225","2048 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Ali, who said: My opinion and Umar's opinion agreed upon freeing slave-mothers of children; then when I took charge I judged that they be enslaved. Abidah said: The opinion of Umar and Ali in unity is dearer to me than the opinion of Ali alone in division."
"3226","2049 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Umar ibn Dharr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Qarib al-Thaqafi, from his father, that he bought a slavegirl who miscarried by him, then he sold her; he mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: 'After your bloods and their bloods, and your fleshes and their fleshes, have mingled, you sold them? Return her, return her.'"
"3227","2050 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, freed slave-mothers of children and mothers of miscarriages.'"
"3228","2051 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Ikrimah, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'When a slavegirl bears a child by her master, she is freed, even if it is a miscarriage.'"
"3229","2052 - Sa'id narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Umar said: 'There is no man who would acknowledge that he used to have intercourse with his slavegirl, then dies, except that she is freed when she bears a child, even if it is a miscarriage.'"
"3230","2053 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', who said: Two men met Ibn Umar at al-Abwa and said to him: We left this man selling slave-mothers of children, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr; so Ibn Umar said: 'Do you know Abu Hafs? For he ruled concerning slave-mothers of children: they are neither sold nor given away; her owner enjoys her, and when he dies she is free.'"
"3231","2054 - Sa'id informed us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that a party met him at al-Abwa and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman; they asked him, meaning about slave-mothers of children; so Abd Allah said: 'You know Umar?' They said: Yes. He said: 'He ruled concerning them that their masters enjoy them as long as they wish, and when the master perishes there is no sale of them nor inheritance.'"
"3232","2055 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Atiyyah Malik ibn Amir al-Hamdani, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said concerning a slave-mother of a child: 'If she accepts Islam, becomes chaste and upright, she is freed; and if she disbelieves, commits immorality and betrays, she is enslaved.'"
"3233","2056 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated: Hushaym informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, concerning a slave-mother of a man's child who apostatized from Islam; he wrote about that to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Umar wrote: 'That they sell her in a land in which there is none of her religion.'"
"3234","2057 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: When a slavegirl miscarries by her master and its form is distinct, she is a slave-mother of a child; and if its form is not distinct, she remains a slavegirl as before."
"3235","2058 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Dawud informed us, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: 'When it turns in the fourth stage of formation and is formed, the waiting period of a free woman ends and a slavegirl is freed thereby.'"
"3236","2059 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Shihab narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, who said: 'When a woman miscarries a distinct fetus, her waiting period has ended.'"
"3237","2060 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a slave-mother of a child; he said: 'Sell her as you sell your sheep or your camel.'"
"3238","2061 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: A man of ours died leaving a slave-mother of a child, and al-Walid ibn Uqbah wanted to sell her for his debt; so they came to Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud while he was praying, and when he finished they mentioned that to him, and he said: 'If it must be, then assign her as part of her children's share.'"
"3239","2062 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said: Any man who has intercourse with his slavegirl then neglects her, the neglect is upon him, and the child is his child."
"3240","2063 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'Make these slavegirls chaste; no man shall have intercourse with his slavegirl then deny her child except that I attach it to him.'"
"3241","2064 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Awwam informed us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that Umar passed by boys at a well drawing water, and with them was a slavegirl drawing with them, so he said: 'Ha, perhaps the owner of this one has intercourse with her then sends her out among what you see; yet if she brings a child we shall attach him to him.'"
"3242","2065 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus narrated, from al-Hasan, who said: 'If a man denies his child by his slavegirl, that is his right.'"
"3243","2066 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to say: 'He may disavow his child when it is by his slavegirl whenever he wishes.'"
"3244","2067 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said that; he said: Even if he takes hold of his beard."
"3245","2068 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man of Kindah used to visit a slavegirl, so she became pregnant and gave birth on his bed; he was congratulated for the child and acknowledged him, then he wanted to sell the slavegirl after that, so she disputed with him before Shurayh; Shurayh said to her: 'Your proof that you gave birth on his bed and that he acknowledged your child.' So she brought proof of that, and he attached the child to him and said: 'He has no right to disavow him.'"
"3246","2069 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to say: 'If he disavows his child when it is by a slavegirl, that is his right; and if it is by a free woman, its mother is put to imprecation (li'an).'"
"3247","2070 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'If he acknowledges his child he has no right to disavow him; and if he disavows him he is lashed the hadd punishment and the child is attached to him.'"
"3248","2071 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah, that Zayd ibn Thabit had a Persian slavegirl from whom he practiced withdrawal; she brought a child, so he freed the child and lashed her the hadd punishment, and said: 'I only sought pleasure with you and did not want you (for childbearing).'"
"3249","2072 - Sa'id informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Kharijah, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit had a Persian slavegirl with whom he had intercourse, and she used to attend to him with grief; she became pregnant, and he said: 'By whom are you pregnant?' She said: By you. He said: 'You lie; a life has been killed - nothing of mine that causes pregnancy ever reached you; I have intercourse with you only to please you, because you attend to me with grief. When she delivered, he lashed her and freed her child.'"
"3250","2073 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from a youth of the people of Medina, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, used to practice withdrawal from a slavegirl of his; she became pregnant, which distressed him, and he said: 'O Allah, do not attach to the family of Umar one who is not of them, for the family of Umar has no obscurity.' She gave birth to a black child, so he said: 'By whom did you deliver?' She said: By the camel-herdsman. So he praised Allah and glorified Him."
"3251","Chapter: a woman who gives birth at six months. 2074 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that a woman gave birth at six months, so she was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he intended to stone her; Ali said to him: That is not yours: Allah Almighty says in His Book: 'And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months.' So it may be six months in the womb and suckling twenty-four months; that completes what Allah said: thirty months. So Umar released her."
"3252","2075 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from the guide of Ibn Abbas, who said: Uthman was brought a woman who gave birth in six months, so he ordered her stoning; Ibn Abbas said: Bring me close to him, so they brought him close, and he said: She disputes with you by the Book of Allah: Allah Almighty says: 'And mothers suckle their children two full years,' and He says in another verse: 'And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months.' So Uthman returned her and released her."
"3253","2076 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Abu Sufyan, who said: Our elders narrated to us that a man went out in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and was absent from his wife for two years; he came while she was pregnant, so he raised her to Umar ibn al-Khattab, who ordered her stoning; Mu'adh said to him: 'If there is a way against her, there is no way for you against what is in her belly.' So Umar detained her until she delivered; she bore a boy with two front teeth, and when the man saw him he said: My son, my son. That reached Umar, and he said: 'Women are unable to bear one like Mu'adh; were it not for Mu'adh, Umar would have perished.'"
"3254","2077 - Sa'id informed us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Jamilah bint Sa'd, from A'ishah, who said: 'A woman does not exceed two years in pregnancy, nor as much as the shifting of the shadow of the stick of this spindle.'"
"3255","2078 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Abu Zibyan, who said: An insane woman was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab and he ordered her stoning; she was passed by Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with boys following her, and he said: What is this? They said: An insane woman committed fornication, and Umar ordered her stoning. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Stay as you are, do not hasten. He came to Umar and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, do you not know that the pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, the insane until he recovers, and the minor until he attains?' Umar said: It is so. Ali said to Umar: 'Then return her and release her.'"
"3256","2079 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'The pen is lifted from four: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the minor until he attains puberty, from the insane until it is unveiled from him, and from the aged who lacks reason.'"
"3257","2080 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Awwam informed us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: An afflicted woman who had committed fornication was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he intended to beat her; Ali said: That is not yours; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The pen is lifted from three: from the minor until he attains puberty, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the insane until it is unveiled from him.' So Umar released her."
"3258","2081 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abu al-Duha, from Ali, similar to that."
"3259","2082 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Umar and Ali, similar to that."
"3260","2083 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Duha, who said: A woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I committed adultery. He kept turning her away until she confessed or testified four times, then he ordered her stoning; Ali said to him: 'Ask her what her adultery is; perhaps she has an excuse?' So he asked her, and she said: I went out with my family's camels, and we had a neighbor; he went out with his camels, and I carried water with me, but there was no milk among my camels, while my neighbor carried water and had milk among his camels; my water ran out, so I asked him for water, but he refused to give me drink unless I yield myself to him; I refused, but when my soul was about to depart I yielded to him. Ali said: 'Allah is Greatest; I see an excuse for her: Whoever is compelled, neither desiring nor transgressing, there is no sin upon him.' So he released her."
"3261","2084 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Hajjaj informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he saw no harm in a slave taking a concubine when his master permits him."
"3262","2085 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in that."
"3263","2086 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Hajjaj informed us, from al-Abbas ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas, from his uncle Ibn Abbas, that he permitted a slave of his to take a concubine; he bought three slavegirls, then two thousand by two thousand. [Flag: price phrase garbled in source]"
"3264","2087 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, that he said to a slave of his: 'So-and-so is yours - a slavegirl of his - so take her.'"
"3265","2088 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Zakariyya ibn Yunus informed us - al-Sa'igh doubted - from al-Sha'bi, that he saw no harm in a slave taking a concubine with his master's permission."
"3266","2089 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Abu Bishr informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that a slave of his bought two slavegirls and used to have intercourse with them, and Ibn Umar knew of that and approved it."
"3267","2090 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that he liked it to be a marriage."
"3268","2091 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say that."
"3269","2092 - Sa'id informed us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Abu Abd Allah al-Shaqari, from Ibrahim, who said: 'It is disliked for a slave to take a concubine.'"
"3270","Chapter: whoever says that a slavegirl appears and prays without a head-cover. 2093 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabi'ah inform Abu al-Sha'tha, who said: My father asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, about the hadd of a slavegirl; Umar said: 'The slavegirl has cast her head-covering from behind the house.' Sufyan said another time: From behind the wall."
"3271","2094 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, from Hajjaj, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: 'The slavegirl has cast the covering of her head behind the wall.'"
"3272","2095 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he was asked about a slavegirl, how she prays? He said: 'She prays in the attire in which she goes out to the market.'"
"3273","2096 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Umar would not leave a slavegirl veiled in his caliphate, and he said: 'That is only for free women, lest they be harmed.'"
"3274","2097 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from Mujahid, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A slavegirl who has menstruated goes out in a waist-wrapper? He said: 'Yes.' I said: How is that? He said: 'People then were needy.' I said: Allah has widened for us. He said: 'Leave me alone.'"
"3275","2098 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Simak, from Ibrahim, who said: 'A slave-mother of a child prays without a head-cover, even if she is sixty years old.'"
"3276","2099 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus narrated, from al-Hasan, that he liked for a slavegirl, when her master assigns her, to pray fully covered."
"3277","Chapter: the waiting period of one pregnant with two children. 2100 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who used to say: 'When a man divorces his wife while in her belly are two children, and she bears one of them, her waiting period has ended.'"
"3278","2101 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'He may take her back so long as she has not delivered the other.'"
"3279","2102 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about that, and he said: 'He has more right to her so long as she has not delivered the other; it is only like menstruation.' Then he said: 'O Abu Husayn, put it in the register.'"
"3280","2103 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'He may take her back so long as she has not delivered the other.'"
"3281","2104 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, Ash'ath narrated, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, who said: 'When she delivers the first, she is separated.'"
"3282","2105 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ash'ath narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, the same as that."
"3283","2106 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Ikrimah, who said: 'When she delivers the first, she is separated.' Sa'id said: Until she delivers the other."
"3284","Chapter: what has come concerning a woman who accepts Islam before her husband. 2107 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter Zaynab to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' when he accepted Islam after Zaynab's Islam, returning her to him by the first marriage."
"3285","2108 - Sa'id informed us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Zaynab bint Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was under Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi'; she accepted Islam before him, and he was captured and brought captive in fetters, then he accepted Islam, so they remained upon their marriage."
"3286","2109 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, Hajjaj narrated, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab, his daughter, to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' with a new marriage."
"3287","2110 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abu Hubayrah al-Ansari, who said: 'When the seventy of the Ansar returned from al-Aqabah, having accepted Islam, and came to Medina, they invited their wives to Islam; they answered them and accepted Islam, so they remained upon their first marriage.'"
"3288","Chapter: whoever is unable to free then fasts part of what is due upon him, then becomes able. 2111 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning one upon whom is a neck (freeing a slave) for zihar, who does not find a neck and fasts a month or so, then becomes able; he said: 'He breaks the fast and frees.' Then he said after that: He continues his fast and does not free."
"3289","2112 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'When he becomes able before finishing the fast, he leaves the fast and freeing becomes obligatory upon him.'"
"3290","Chapter: husband and wife dispute over the dower. 2113 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'When husband and wife dispute over the dower, the word is the husband's with his oath, and proof is upon the wife.' Al-Shaybani said: Hammad narrated to us from Ibrahim that he used to say: 'The word is hers within the dower of her peers.' Hushaym said: The word is what al-Sha'bi said."
"3291","Chapter: a man finds his wife not a virgin. 2114 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan; and Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim; and al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, that they said concerning a man when he does not find his wife a virgin; they said: 'Nothing is upon him; virginity departs without suspicion - leaping removes it, and much menstruation, and spinsterhood, and a heavy load.'"
"3292","2115 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who consummated with his wife and said: I did not find her a virgin; he said: 'Nothing is upon him; virginity is removed by leaping, and a heavy load.'"
"3293","2116 - Sa'id informed us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ma'mar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, who said: I asked Salim ibn Abd Allah: A man says to his wife: I did not find you a virgin? He said: 'It is nothing; virginity is removed by leaping and menstruation.'"
"3294","2117 - Sa'id informed us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, the same as that."
"3295","2118 - Sa'id informed us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yunus, from Yazid, from al-Zuhri, that a man married a woman and did not find her a virgin; menstruation had burned away her virginity, so A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, sent to him: 'Menstruation removes virginity certainly.'"
"3296","Chapter: two men marry two sisters, and each consummates with the other's wife. 2119 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Muhammad ibn Salim narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning two brothers who married two sisters, and each one's brother's wife was brought to him; he said: 'They are separated, and each of them has the dower; neither of them shall approach his wife until the waiting period of her sister ends, and the two husbands shall claim the dower from whoever deceived them.'"
"3297","2120 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan; and Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that both said that."
"3298","Chapter: a woman testified against for adultery then found a virgin. 2121 - Sa'id informed us, Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said concerning a woman against whom four testify of adultery, then she is examined and found a virgin; al-Sha'bi said: 'I would not carry out a hadd upon a woman upon whom is a seal from Allah.'"
"3299","2122 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Isma'il informed us, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: 'The hadd is carried out upon her, and no attention is paid to that in her.' Hushaym said: And it is the opinion."
"3300","2123 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'There is no hadd upon a repentant one.'"
"3301","2124 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Bayan, from Amir al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard him say: 'When a man marries a virgin and her husband accuses her before consummating with her, and women look at her and find her a virgin, he is lashed, because it is clear he lied against her.'"
"3302","2125 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled concerning a virgin woman whom an old shaykh married, and she became pregnant; the shaykh claimed he had not had intercourse with her, and she was asked: Did he deflower you? She said: No. He ordered women to examine her, and they claimed she was a virgin. He said: 'A woman has two passages: the passage of menstruation and the passage of urine; perhaps the man would ejaculate at her front in the passage of menstruation, so she became pregnant.' The man was asked, and he said: I used to ejaculate the fluid at her front. It was said to the shaykh: She remains as she is, and the pregnancy is yours, and its child is yours. [Flag: 'she remains' phrase truncated in source]"
"3303","Chapter: a man claims a child from adultery. 2126 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: 'Whoever claims a child from adultery is not believed, it is not attached to him, and it does not inherit from him.'"
"3304","2127 - Sa'id informed us, Salamah ibn Hazzal narrated, who said: I bowed two rak'ahs at the Station in Mecca, when Tawus was at my right; a tailor asked him about a man who had intercourse with a woman unlawfully and she bore him a child, then he married her and she bore him a child - which of the two inherits from him? He said: 'His legitimate child inherits from him, and the other inherits nothing from him.'"
"3305","2128 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Mecca, saying: He has a child from the mother of so-and-so from adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Woe to you; there is no illicit intercourse in Islam; the child is for the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone of disgrace.'"
"3306","2129 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent for an old man in their house; he said: So I went with him, and he asked him about children of pre-Islamic births. He said: As for the semen, it is so-and-so's, and as for the bed, it is so-and-so's. Umar said: You spoke truthfully, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled by the bed."
"3307","2130 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zam'ah disputed over the son of Zam'ah's slavegirl; Sa'd said: My brother Utbah bequeathed to me: When you come to Mecca, take the son of Zam'ah's slavegirl, for he is his son. Abd ibn Zam'ah said: My brother, the son of my father's slavegirl, born on my father's bed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a clear resemblance to Utbah, and said: 'The child is for the bed; and veil yourself from him, O Sawdah.'"
"3308","2131 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The child is for the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.'"
"3309","2132 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The child is for the bed, and in the mouth of the adulterer is the stone.'"
"3310","Chapter: what a widow in her waiting period must avoid. 2133 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking permission for kohl, because her husband had died; he did not permit her, and said: 'One of you used to throw the dung after a year; now it is only four months and ten days.'"
"3311","2134 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Salamah, that she was asked about a widow: May she apply ithmid kohl in her waiting period? She said: 'No, even if her eyes burst; but with aloe (sabr) and powder (dharur).'"
"3312","2135 - Sa'id informed us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated, from Ibn Sirin and Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, that she said concerning a widow: 'She shall touch no dye, nor apply kohl, nor wear a dyed garment, nor touch perfume except a bit of costus (qust) and nails (azfar) at her purity.'"
"3313","2136 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that when the news of Abu Sufyan came to Umm Habibah, she called for yellow perfume after the third day, wiped her cheeks and forearms with it, and said: I had no need of this, were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a dead one except for a husband; she mourns him four months and ten days.'"
"3314","2137 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he said concerning a widow: 'She shall touch no dye, nor perfume, nor kohl, nor a dyed garment except an 'asb cloth she wraps herself with; and she shall not spend the night outside her house until her waiting period ends.'"
"3315","2138 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', that Safiyyah, the wife of Abd Allah, when Abd Allah died leaving her, complained of her eyes, and she would drip aloe (sabr) into them."
"3316","2139 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he said concerning a widow: 'She shall not apply beautifying kohl except with aloe or powder; she shall not spend the night outside her house, nor go out for visiting the sick or kin; and one divorced thrice is the same.'"
"3317","2140 - Sa'id informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: Urwah was of the strictest of people in mourning. A woman asked him: May she wear a head-cover dyed with baqqam while mourning? He said: 'No.' She said: By Allah, I have none other. He said: 'Then dye it black.' Urwah said: 'The Sunnah in mourning is that a woman may not mourn beyond three days; when it is the fourth day she is ordered that yellowness or saffron touch her garment. A woman mourning her husband shall touch nothing until her term ends.'"
"3318","2141 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who married a woman and divorced her before consummating with her; her guardian pardoned half the dower, so she disputed with her husband before Shurayh, who said: 'Your guardian has pardoned.' Then he retracted from that afterward, making the one in whose hand is the marriage tie the husband."
"3319","2142 - Sa'id informed us, Isa ibn Yunus and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: 'It is the guardian.' Shurayh used to say: 'It is the husband.'"
"3320","Chapter: what is lawful for a man of his wife when she is menstruating. 2143 - Sa'id informed us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali, from Asim ibn Amr, who said: A party of the people of Iraq went out to Umar ibn al-Khattab; he asked them: 'From where are you?' They said: From the people of Iraq. He said: 'Did you come with my permission?' They said: Yes. They asked him what is lawful for a man of his wife while she is menstruating, about washing from janabah, and about a man's prayer in his house. He said to them: 'Are you sorcerers?' They said: No by Allah, we are no sorcerers. He said: 'You have asked me about qualities none asked me of all of them together after I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except you. As for what is lawful for a man of his wife while she is menstruating, it is what is above the waist-wrapper; as for a man's prayer in his house, it is light, so lighten your houses; and as for washing from janabah, perform the ablution of prayer, then wash your head three times, then pour over the rest of your body.'"
"3321","2144 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Layth narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, that A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, was asked: What is for a man of his wife when she menstruates? She said: 'What is above the waist-wrapper.'"
"3322","2145 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from A'ishah, who said: 'I would wrap myself while menstruating, and enter with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into his blanket.'"
"3323","2146 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from A'ishah, that she used to sleep with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a blanket while she was menstruating."
"3324","2147 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan; and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, who both said: 'When the private part is covered, there is no harm in anything besides that.'"
"3325","2148 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Shihab narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, who said: 'A man may place his member on a menstruating woman wherever he wishes, so long as he does not insert it.'"
"3326","Chapter: comprehensive divorce. 2149 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah narrated, from Ibrahim, that a man had an orphan girl with him who used to attend his food; his wife feared he would marry her besides her, so the man was absent for a time, and the wife sought the help of women against the slavegirl; they beat her up for her and spoiled her virginity. He said: The man returned and began to miss the slavegirl at his table and food; the man said to his wife: What is the state of so-and-so, she does not attend my food? She said: Leave so-and-so alone. He said: What is her matter? She said: She committed fornication. He went to her, and when he entered to her he said: What is your matter? She began to weep. He said: Then inform me. So she informed him. He went to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him; Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sent for the man's wife and the women, and no sooner had they come to him than they confessed what they had done. He said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: Judge in it, O Hasan. He said: 'The hadd is upon whoever accused her, and the bride-price is upon her and the holders.' Ali said: If flour-laden camels were tasked they would grind, though no camel grinds that day. [Flag: final proverb obscure in source]"
"3327","2150 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, al-Sha'bi informed us, that four slavegirls gathered; one of them said: She is a man, another said: She is a woman, the third said: She is the father of the one who claimed she is a man, and the fourth said: She is the father of the one who claimed she is a woman. The one who claimed she is the father of the man proposed to the other who claimed she is the father of the woman, and they married her to him. The one who claimed she is a man set upon the other and deflowered her with her finger. That was raised to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, who placed the dower upon them in quarters, dropping the share of the one who claimed she is a woman because she yielded herself. We mentioned that to Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil al-Muzani, who said: 'Had I ruled, I would have placed the dower upon the one who spoiled the slavegirl alone.'"
"3328","2151 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Abu Bishr informed us, from Abu Rawh Shabib al-Shami, that a man used to rendezvous with a woman at a place where he would come to her; another woman learned of that and sat in that place; the man came and had intercourse with her thinking she was his slavegirl. When he finished, he looked and she was not his slavegirl. He came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him; Umar sent to Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and Ali said: 'Lash the man the hadd in secret, and lash the woman the hadd in public.'"
"3329","2152 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yazid ibn Barrad, the freedman of Bajilah, informed us; he said: I heard al-Sha'bi concerning two men who testified against a man that he divorced his wife; the judge separated the man and his wife, then one of the two witnesses married her, and the other retracted his testimony. Al-Sha'bi said: 'The judgment stands, and no attention is paid to the word of the one who retracted.'"
"3330","2153 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mansur narrated, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who says to his wife: You are freed, intending divorce; he said: 'It is one, and he has more right to her.'"
"3331","2154 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'A slave begins spending upon his family before his yield to his masters.'"
"3332","2155 - Sa'id informed us, Sharik narrated, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'A slave begins spending upon his wife before his yield to his masters.'"
"3333","2156 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a man under whom is a mukatabah (contracted slavegirl); he strove with her and aided her until she fulfilled her contract. He said: 'She has no choice.'"
"3334","2157 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated, Yunus narrated, from al-Hasan, who said: 'When a man has intercourse with his mukatabah, there shall be reckoned for her the dower of her peers from her contract.'"
"3335","2158 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated: Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, then he was ordered to take her back."
"3336","2159 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he was asked about a man whose slave-girl commits fornication and gives birth from fornication: may he sell her child and consume its price? Al-Hasan said: ""He is like part of his wealth."""
"3337","2160 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, that a man was on a roof and called his wife, but she delayed coming to him, so he said to her: Come, and when you come then choose; so she came and said: I choose myself. He said: I did not mean that; I only gave you a choice between sitting and going back. Abdullah ibn Ma'qil was asked about that and said: ""He is judged by his intention."""
"3338","2161 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to consider nothing of what a man grants his wife at the unveiling (consummation) as anything (binding)."
"3339","2162 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to consider nothing of a (marital) gift valid except what was delivered intact."
"3340","2163 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from al-Hasan, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, and she claimed she married (another) husband who consummated marriage with her. He said: ""If she is deemed truthful in his view, let him marry her if he wishes; and if she is suspect in his view, let him ask about that and investigate it."""
"3341","2164 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, he said: A man came and said: His mother kept pressing him until he married, then she later said to him: Divorce her. Al-Hasan said to him: ""Divorcing your wife is in no way part of dutifulness to your mother."""
"3342","2165 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, and from one of our companions, from Ibrahim, that they both said concerning a slave who has a free woman under him (as wife), consummated marriage with her, then was freed, then committed indecency: ""There is no stoning upon him until he consummates with his wife after emancipation, and he is flogged."""
"3343","2166 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that he used to see no harm in a man giving gifts to his wife during her waiting period if he intended to marry her."
"3344","2167 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, that a man forced a woman until he tore her (causing injury) and deflowered her, so that was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he flogged him the prescribed hadd and imposed on him one-third of her blood-money."
"3345","2168 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Umar informed us, Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For a man to be struck a blow that reaches the bone of his head is better for him than for a woman to place her hand on his forearm, when she is not lawful for him."""
"3346","2169 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Umm Musa, she said: ""When the people of Madinah wanted to present a slave-girl bride to her husband, she would be taken to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), supplication would be made for her, then she would be taken to her husband."""
"3347","2170 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Umm Musa, that Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, when he gave one of his daughters in marriage, used to command her to good character, and he used to consider that good."
"3348","2171 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Umm Musa, that an umm walad (a slave-mother of a child) of Abdullah ibn Ja'far passed by Ali while she was pregnant, so he wiped her belly and said: ""O Allah, make him a male, blessed."""
"3349","2172 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Shubrumah informed us, he said: I was with al-Sha'bi when a man came to him and said to him: He vowed to divorce his wife. Al-Sha'bi said: ""Expiate your oath and do not divorce your wife."" I said to myself: If I refute the shaykh's statement there is something grave in that, and if I remain silent something I dislike will befall me; so I said: O Abu Amr, divorce is disobedience, yet he said what he said. So he woke up (to the point), said: Bring me the man; so he was brought, and he said: ""Your vow remains upon your neck until the Day of Resurrection unless you divorce your wife."""
"3350","2173 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, he said: ""They used to treat co-wives equally; and if some flour or parched barley remained that could not be measured, they divided it by handfuls."""
"3351","2174 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: ""Mu'adh ibn Jabal had two wives; when it was the day of one of them he would not perform ablution from the house of the other. They both died on the same day, so he buried them in one grave, and drew lots between them as to which of them would enter the grave first."""
"3352","2175 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who died while in a rented house, he said: ""It is best that she observe her waiting period in the house she was in, and the rent be paid."""
"3353","2176 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about something concerning divorce. He said: ""A man was asked: How many times did you divorce your wife? So he gestured with his hand three or four, pointing with his hand without speaking; so she became separated (divorced) by three."""
"3354","2177 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who marries his umm walad to his slave, he said: ""The slave shall not have intercourse with her until she menstruates one menstruation."""
"3355","2178 - Sa'id informed us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from Ata, concerning a man who owns a slave-girl and learns she commits fornication, he said: ""There is no harm in having intercourse with her."""
"3356","2179 - Sa'id informed us, Khalid informed us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who makes a settlement with his wife over a settlement regarding her day (turn), then she retracts, he said: ""If she consented, she has no right to retract."""
"3357","2180 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, who heard Bajalah narrating to Amr ibn Aws and Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: I was a scribe for Jaz' ibn Mu'awiyah, the uncle of al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, when the letter of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, came a year before his death: ""Kill every sorcerer, separate the Magians from their unlawful kinswomen, and forbid them humming (their murmured rites)."" So we killed three sorceresses, and separated a man from his unlawful kinswoman according to the Book of Allah; and he prepared food, then invited the Magians, placing the sword upon his thigh, so they ate without humming, and they delivered a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver. Umar ibn al-Khattab had not taken jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"3358","2181 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Awf ibn Abbad al-Mazini narrated to us, from Bajalah ibn Abdah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari: ""Separate the Magians from their unlawful kinswomen so that we attach them to the People of the Book, and kill every sorcerer and soothsayer."""
"3359","2182 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, Qays ibn Amr informed us, from Bajalah ibn Abdah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari: ""Strike the humming ones (to stop their murmuring) until they speak, separate every Magian man from his unlawful kinswoman, and kill the sorcerers."""
"3360","2183 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Fudayl al-Raqashi, sixty years ago, say: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Adi ibn Artah: Ask al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan: Why did the early Muslims affirm the marriages of sisters and mothers (among the Magians)? Al-Hasan said: ""Because when al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami came to Bahrayn he left the people upon this."""
"3361","2184 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: ""A slave may marry four (women)."""
"3362","2185 - Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, he said: ""Two."""
"3363","2186 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Talhah, Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""A slave marries two (women) and divorces with two divorces, and a slave-girl observes a waiting period of two menstruations; if she does not menstruate, then a month and a half - or he said - two months."" Sufyan doubted."
"3364","2187 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, ""uncovered his slave-girl and looked at her, then forbade one of his sons to approach her."""
"3365","2188 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, the two sons of Amir ibn Rabi'ah - and their father was a Badr veteran - that he bequeathed concerning a slave-girl of his that they sell her and not approach her, as though he had seen something of her that he disliked, so he disliked that they see of her what he had seen."
"3366","2189 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Rabi'ah, that his father Rabi'ah was a Badr veteran; he bequeathed concerning a slave-girl of his that his sons not approach her, and said: ""I took nothing of her except that I looked a look (I regretted), and I dislike that you look at her (likewise)."""
"3367","2190 - Sa'id informed us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Masruq said in the illness in which he died: ""My slave-girl is not forbidden to you except for touching and looking."" And she used to attend to him."
"3368","2191 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, that Masruq said to his slave-girl at his death: ""I took nothing of her except that her inviolability forbids touching and looking to my son."""
"3369","2192 - Sa'id informed us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: ""If the father uncovers her (looks at her nakedness), he forbids her to the son; and if the son uncovers her, he forbids her to the father."""
"3370","2193 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: ""A father forbids (her) to his son by kissing her, or placing his hand on her private part, or his private part upon hers, or embracing her intimately."""
"3371","2194 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: ""They used to consider the kiss and touch as forbidding (making unlawful) the mother and the daughter."""
"3372","2195 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Yazid, he said: I had a slave-girl I used to have intercourse with, and she had a little daughter just past weaning; I drew her to me while she was naked and felt desire in myself, so I asked al-Hasan, and he said: ""Do not approach her mother."""
"3373","2196 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: ""If a man touches a slave-girl's private part, or his private part touches hers, she becomes forbidden to his father and his son."""
"3374","2197 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, concerning the clearance (istibra) of a slave-girl when a man buys her, he said: ""If she does not menstruate, he clears her (womb) in forty-five (days); and if she menstruates, then two menstruations."""
"3375","2198 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: ""A slave-girl is cleared (for istibra) with one menstruation."""
"3376","2199 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he was asked about clearing (istibra of) a slave-girl who has not reached menstruation. He said: ""Clear her with three months."" That was denied, so we went to Ibn Sirin and asked him, and he said the same as al-Hasan said; and he said once: that was denied, so they went to Ibn Sirin and he said the same as al-Hasan said."
"3377","2200 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from al-Hakam, he said: ""He clears (her) with three months."""
"3378","2201 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Qilabah, that he said: ""She is cleared with three months."""
"3379","2202 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz asked the people of Madinah and the midwives, and they said: ""A pregnant woman is not cleared in less than three months."" Sufyan said, from Sadaqah, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz was pleased with the saying of the people of Madinah: she is cleared with three months."
"3380","2203 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: ""She is cleared with a month and a half."""
"3381","2204 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, he said: ""She is cleared with a month and a half."""
"3382","2205 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, he said: She is cleared with a month and a half."
"3383","2206 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning a slave-girl when she is sold, he said: ""The seller clears her with one menstruation, and the buyer with one menstruation."""
"3384","2207 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur and Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, that he used to say: ""She is cleared with one menstruation,"" then he said afterwards: with two menstruations."
"3385","2208 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say concerning a man who buys a slave-girl while she is menstruating, he said: ""He shall not approach her until she menstruates one menstruation in his possession."""
"3386","2209 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: He may suffice himself with that menstruation."
"3387","2210 - Sa'id informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who bought a slave-girl from some people, he said: ""He shall clear her (womb)."""
"3388","2211 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, that they both used to say: ""If a man buys a slave-girl while she is pregnant, he shall not approach her until she delivers what is in her belly."""
"3389","2212 - Sa'id informed us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, concerning a man who buys a slave-girl, he said: He shall not touch her nor place his hand upon her until he clears her (womb)."
"3390","2213 - Sa'id informed us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: ""He may enjoy of her whatever he wishes so long as he does not touch her private part."""
"3391","2214 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to see no harm in a man enjoying of a slave-girl he is clearing (for istibra) short of the private part. He said: And Ibn Sirin used to dislike that."
"3392","2215 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, the like of the hadith of Hushaym."
"3393","2216 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: ""They used to compel the slave to marry, and enter him with his wife into the house, and close the door upon them."""
"3394","2217 - Sa'id informed us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus (azl). He said: ""Do you do that? There is no harm upon you in doing it; indeed there is no soul decreed by Allah except that it will come into being."""
"3395","2218 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Qaza'ah informed me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Coitus interruptus was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Why would one of you do that?"" And he did not say: Let him not do that. ""For there is no created soul except that Allah is its Creator."""
"3396","2219 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Sa'id informed us, Abu al-Waddak Jabr ibn Nawf narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: We took captives and wanted to ransom them, so we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: A man has a slave-girl, he enjoys her and practices coitus interruptus with her for fear she conceive from him. He said: ""Do what seems fit to you, for whatever matter is decreed will be, even if you dislike it."""
"3397","2220 - Sa'id informed us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: ""There is no harm upon you in not doing it; if it be of what Allah took the covenant upon, though it were upon this rock, Allah will bring it forth."""
"3398","2221 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Mas'ud was asked about coitus interruptus, and said: ""There is no harm upon you in not doing it; for if that drop from which Allah took the covenant were in a rock, He would breathe the spirit into it."""
"3399","2222 - Sa'id informed us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrated to me, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he said concerning coitus interruptus: ""It is the minor burial alive (of a female infant)."""
"3400","2223 - Sa'id informed us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said concerning coitus interruptus: ""That is the hidden burial alive."""
"3401","2224 - Sa'id informed us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abbad Abi Hubayrah, that Khabbab ibn al-Aratt used to practice coitus interruptus with his concubines."
"3402","2225 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, he said: Umm Ata narrated to me, from an umm walad of Khabbab, that Khabbab used to practice coitus interruptus with her."
"3403","2226 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, who heard Sulayman ibn Yasar say: Sa'd passed through the mosque, so his brother asked him about coitus interruptus, and he said: ""We used to dislike it until Zayd ibn Thabit claimed there is no harm in it."""
"3404","2227 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, from a man, that Zayd ibn Thabit was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: Say, O Hajjaj: ""It is your tilth; if you wish you water it, and if you wish you leave it thirsty."""
"3405","2228 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: ""It is your tilth; if you wish then water it, and if you wish then leave it thirsty."""
"3406","2229 - Sa'id informed us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Umar and Ibn Umar used to dislike coitus interruptus, while Zayd ibn Thabit and Ibn Mas'ud used to practice coitus interruptus."
"3407","2230 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: ""Umar and Uthman used to dislike coitus interruptus, and they used to say: Whoever has intercourse then stops short (without ejaculation/incompletion), ghusl is upon him; while men of the Ansar used to see no harm in coitus interruptus, and they used to say: Whoever has intercourse then stops short, there is no ghusl upon him."""
"3408","2231 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from one who narrated to him, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to practice coitus interruptus with an umm walad of his, then she bore a child, so he recognized the resemblance and acknowledged him."
"3409","2232 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that he struck one of his sons over coitus interruptus, and he used to dislike it."
"3410","2233 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas had a black slave-girl, and he used to have intercourse with her and practice coitus interruptus with her, placing his fluid in a cloth and showing it to her."
"3411","2234 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about coitus interruptus, and he said: ""Ibn Umar used to dislike it; and from Ibn Abbas: he saw no harm in it."""
"3412","2235 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, he said: An umm walad of Sa'd narrated to me that Sa'd used to practice coitus interruptus with her."
"3413","2236 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Sa'd, that he used to practice coitus interruptus."
"3414","2237 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Salim informed us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, that a man asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about his wife while she is menstruating, whether he may practice coitus interruptus with her for fear of a child, and he permitted him that."
"3415","2238 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: ""He seeks the permission of the free woman, and does not seek the permission of the slave-girl."""
"3416","2239 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he said the like of that."
"3417","2240 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: ""What is it to you that you withhold that?"""
"3418","2241 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: ""He practices coitus interruptus with the slave-girl, and seeks the permission of the free woman."""
"3419","2242 - Sa'id narrated to us, - I think Sufyan - narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he said: ""Sa'd and Zayd ibn Thabit used to practice coitus interruptus."""
"3420","2243 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir, he said: A man of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a servant-girl who draws water upon a camel of mine, and I practice coitus interruptus with her, yet she became pregnant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever Allah has decreed to create, it will surely be."""
"3421","2244 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning the scattering of sugar (at weddings), he said: ""They used to take it for the children."""
"3422","2245 - Sa'id informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, that he disliked it."
"3423","2246 - Sa'id informed us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abdullah al-Khatmi, he said: I witnessed Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla at a wedding feast; they brought sugar and wanted to scatter it, so Abd al-Rahman said: ""Put it down, then divide it."""
"3424","2247 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, he said: They asked him about the scattering of sugar. He said: If they put it down, then take it; and if they scatter it, then do not take it."
"3425","2248 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym informed us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us - both narrating to us while sitting together - from Nafi', that a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a slave-girl of his to a slave-boy of his, and he used to go to her secretly; so Umar sent to the man and said: What has your slave-girl so-and-so done? He said: I married her to a slave-boy of mine. He said: ""Do you take of her?"" The people behind Umar gestured to him: Say: No. One of them said: Had you said: Yes, he would have made you an example to the worlds; and the other said: Had you said: Yes, he would have stoned you."
"3426","2249 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Shurayh said: ""I dislike having intercourse with a woman such that, had I found a man with her, I would not establish the hadd upon her."""
"3427","2250 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Shurayh was asked about a slave-girl when she has a husband, and said: ""Two swords in one sheath."""
"3428","2251 - Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud bought a slave-girl from his wife, and she stipulated upon him: if he sells her, she has more right to her for the price. So he asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: ""Do not approach her while anyone has a condition in her."""
"3429","2252 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abdullah bought a slave-girl from his wife, and she stipulated her service; so he asked Umar, and he said: ""Nothing of your wealth is that in which there is a condition for other than you."""
"3430","2253 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to dislike a man buying a slave-girl upon (condition) that there be no sale and no gifting."
"3431","2254 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that they both said: ""The sale is not permitted and the condition is void."""
"3432","2255 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, that was mentioned to him, and he said: ""I wish I could find a slave-girl to buy upon this condition, and grant her emancipation."""
"3433","2256 - Sa'id informed us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: ""I bought a slave-girl with the stipulation upon me that I neither sell nor gift nor give her as dowry, and when I die she is free. So I asked Ata - or he was asked - and he disliked it; and I asked al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, he said: There is no harm in it; and I asked Makhul, and he said: No harm in it. So I said: Do you fear any sin upon me in it? He said: Rather I hope for you reward in it. And I asked Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, and he said: This is an evil private part (a bad bargain)."" Al-Awza'i said: And Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from al-Hasan, he said: The sale is valid and the condition is void; and I asked al-Zuhri, and he informed me that Ibn Mas'ud wrote to Umar asking him about his buying from his wife a slave-girl upon (condition) that if he sells her, she has more right to her for the price; so Umar said: ""Do not tread a private part in which there is a condition for other than you."""
"3434","2257 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Habib ibn Salim, the freedman of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: A woman came to al-Nu'man with her slave-girl, and he said: Indeed I have with me concerning that a decisive report which I narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""If you had permitted him, I strike him one hundred; and if you had not permitted him, I stone him."" The people said to her: Your husband and the father of your child will be stoned; say: I had permitted him; jealousy alone carried me to that. He said: So he struck him one hundred."
"3435","2258 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: Mudrik ibn Umarah ibn Uqbah informed me that a freedwoman of theirs came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, claiming her husband fell upon her slave-girl; so he said: ""If you are truthful, we stone your husband; and if you are lying, we flog you eighty."""
"3436","2259 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Haytham ibn Badr, from Hurqus ibn Bashir al-Dabbi, he said: ""A man who fell upon his wife's slave-girl was brought forth; the man said: She is my wife, and her wealth is my wealth; so he averted the hadd from him, and said: But if you return (I shall punish you)."""
"3437","2260 - Sa'id informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr, from his father, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab averted stoning from a Bedouin man who fell upon his wife's slave-girl, and flogged him one hundred."
"3438","2261 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: A man went out with his wife's slave-girl on a journey; he fell ill and she treated him, and it was as though she saw something of him; so he bought her from himself, then had intercourse with her. When he arrived, his wife went and informed Umar ibn al-Khattab; so Umar said to the man: ""You bought one of your hands with the other; you shall not escape from me from one of the two prescribed punishments."""
"3439","2262 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbiq al-Hudhali, that a man went out on a journey, and his wife sent with him a servant of hers to serve him; so he fell upon her in his journey. When he arrived he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""If you forced her, she is free and upon you is her like to her mistress; and if she obeyed you, she is a slave and upon you is her like."""
"3440","2263 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur and Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan - and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was a bold man, and he used to consider stoning due upon him."
"3441","2264 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man came to Abdullah and said: He had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl. Abdullah said: ""Cover yourself with Allah's covering, repent to Allah, and if you can buy her and free her, do so."" And he saw no hadd upon him."
"3442","2265 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, Masruq narrated to us, that Abdullah came out of his house one day with his house full of people, and said: ""Whoever of you came asking about an inheritance law or a matter that befell him of judgment or other than that, let him step aside; and whoever of you came to inform us of a matter he concealed, let him conceal repentance as he concealed the sin; for we own nothing but li'an (mutual cursing)."" A man of Banu Tamim stood to him and said: His wife - and she is of intertwined lineage in the tribe - used to seek my permission for visiting, either on a day when they perform hajj, or a mourning gathering among them, or the like; she sought my permission one day and I permitted her. When the house was empty for me, I fell upon her slave-girl, and she became pregnant. When the pregnancy became evident, my wife said to me: You are my cousin, and I dislike your disgrace; so bring men of the tribe and make them witness that I have gifted her to you. He said: So I did. What is repentance for what I did, and what is her reward for what she did? Abdullah said: ""Cover yourself with Allah's covering, repent to Allah, and if you can buy her and free her, perhaps that expiates for you what was of you; and as for her reward, give her her like."""
"3443","2266 - Sa'id informed us, Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah said: ""I do not care whether I come to my wife's slave-girl or to the slave-girl of Awsajah"" - a neighbor of his of al-Nakha'."
"3444","2267 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah said: ""I do not care whether I tread my wife's slave-girl or the slave-girl of Awsajah"" - meaning the slave-girl of a neighbor of his."
"3445","2268 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ubaydah informed us, Ibrahim informed us, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: ""An arrow in my quiver is more beloved to me than a beautiful slave-girl of my wife."""
"3446","Chapter: The boy between the two parents - which of them has more right to him. 2269 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Umar saw his son Asim with his grandmother, and Umar had disputed her (for custody); so Abu Bakr said: ""Leave him with her."" And he did not argue the speech with him."
"3447","2270 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that Umar disputed his wife Umm Asim bint Asim concerning his son by her, before Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him; so Abu Bakr said to him: ""Hand him to her."" And he did not argue the speech with him."
"3448","2271 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, that Umar disputed his wife Umm Asim concerning his son by her, before Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both; so Abu Bakr judged for his mother, then said: ""Upon you is his maintenance until he comes of age."""
"3449","2272 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ikrimah, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, judged him for his mother, and said: ""Her scent, her smelling (embrace), and her tenderness are better for him than you."""
"3450","2273 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that Abu Bakr judged him for his mother, and said: Indeed her scent and her lap are better for him than you."
"3451","2274 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Ata, that Abu Bakr swore an oath upon Umar that he leave the boy with his mother; so he left him with her."
"3452","2275 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother."
"3453","2276 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Uthman al-Batti informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salamah al-Ansari informed us, that his grandfather accepted Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you wish, you may give him the choice."" He placed the father on one side and the mother on one side, then gave the boy the choice; so he went toward his mother. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, guide him."" So the boy returned to his father."
"3454","2277 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother."
"3455","2278 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, he said: An orphan boy was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he gave him the choice; he chose his mother and left his uncle. Umar said to him: ""Indeed the hardship of your mother is better for you than the ease of your uncle."" Al-Sa'igh said it with a dal (jadb, hardship)."
"3456","2279 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus al-Jarmi, from Umarah al-Jarmi, I am the one whom Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, gave the choice between his mother and his uncle."
"3457","2280 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from his mother, that her maternal aunt disputed with the paternal kin of her child before Shurayh concerning a daughter and son of hers; so the daughter chose her mother and the boy chose his paternal uncle."
"3458","2281 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus, Ibn Awn, Hisham, and Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, he said: ""The father has more right, and the mother is kinder."""
"3459","2282 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, he said: ""The little girl is with her mother so long as she is with them, and with them of their wealth is what satiates them; but when the abode separates, the guardians have more right."""
"3460","2283 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus and Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Children were brought from al-Sawad whose father died, so Shurayh said: ""Give them the choice; let them be with whom they love."""
"3461","2284 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, he said: A mother and a grandmother disputed before Shurayh. The grandmother said: [Flag: source text garbled/truncated at this point]"
"3462","2285 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar compelled the paternal kin of a child that the men, not the women, spend upon him."
"3463","2286 - Sa'id informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, imposed upon three persons, each of whom inherits the child, the wage of his suckling."
"3464","2287 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from a paternal aunt of his, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Indeed your children are of the purest of your earnings, so eat of your earnings."""
"3465","2288 - Sa'id informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your children are of your earnings, so eat of the wealth of your children."""
"3466","2289 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from A'ishah, the like of that, but he did not mention the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3467","2290 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father has wealth and dependents, and I have wealth and dependents, and he wants to take my wealth and spend it upon his dependents. He said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."""
"3468","2291 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man of the Ansar disputed his father before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My father takes my wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."""
"3469","2292 - Sa'id informed us, Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have wealth and a child, and my father has wealth and a child; he wants to take my wealth to his wealth and his child. He said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."""
"3470","2293 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Hadrami informed us, from Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Each one has more right to his wealth than his child, his parent, and all people."""
"3471","2294 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that a man came to Abu al-Sha'tha, and said: My son withholds his wealth from me. He said: ""Take of his wealth what suffices you in a fair manner."""
"3472","2295 - Sa'id informed us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: By Allah, I heard Muharib ibn Dithar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The child is of the father's earning."""
"3473","Chapter: What has come concerning ill omen. 2296 - Sa'id informed us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani, from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Ta'i, from Mu'awiyah ibn Hakim al-Numayri, from his uncle Hakim ibn Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no ill omen; and blessedness (good fortune) is in the woman, the mount, and the house."""
"3474","2297 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to see no harm in a man seeking a Jewish woman, a Christian woman, or an immoral woman to suckle his child."
"3475","2298 - Sa'id informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibrahim, the like of it, except that he did not mention the immoral woman."
"3476","2299 - Sa'id informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from a man of Kinanah, I think Utwarī, he said: I sat with Ibn Umar, and he said to me: Of the sons of so-and-so are you? I said: No, but they suckled me. He said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: ""Milk transmits resemblance."""
"3477","Book of Jihad. Chapter: What has come concerning the merit of jihad in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic. 2300 - Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, were it not that I would burden the believers, I would never stay behind from any expedition fighting in the way of Allah; but I do not find means, nor do they find strength to follow me, nor would their souls be content to stay behind after me."" Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: ""Contrary to an expedition"" (a variant wording)."
"3478","2301 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani informed me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Sa'id, whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet, Paradise is due for him."" Abu Sa'id marveled at it and said: Repeat it to me, O Messenger of Allah. So he did; then he said: ""And another by which the servant is raised one hundred degrees in Paradise, between every two degrees as between the heaven and the earth."" He said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Jihad in the way of Allah, jihad in the way of Allah, jihad in the way of Allah."""
"3479","2302 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are most excellent? He said: ""Prayer at its time."" I said: Then which? He said: ""Then dutifulness to parents."" I said: Then which? He said: ""Then jihad in the way of Allah."" By Allah, had I asked him for more he would have given me more. I said: Which sins are greatest before Allah? He said: ""That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you."" I said: Then which? He said: ""That you kill your child fearing he eat with you."" I said: Then which? He said: ""That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife."" He said: We remained only a little until Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed its confirmation: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit fornication; and whoever does that shall meet punishment}."
"3480","2303 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani informed me, from Amr ibn Malik, that he heard Fadalah ibn Ubayd narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever dies upon one of these ranks shall be raised upon it on the Day of Resurrection."""
"3481","2304 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abu Hani' informed me, from Amr ibn Malik, that he heard Fadalah ibn Ubayd saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""I am a guarantor - and the guarantor is the surety - for whoever believes in me, submits as a Muslim, emigrates, and strives in the path of Allah, of a house on the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise. Whoever does that has left no pursuit of good unpursued and no escape from evil unesought; he dies wherever he wishes to die."""
"3482","2305 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Zayd ibn Ayman, from Abu Muhammad al-Basri, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, that a man at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had much wealth, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed by which I may reach the deeds of those who strive in the path of Allah. He said: ""How much is your wealth?"" He said: Six thousand dinars. He said: ""Even if you spent it all in obedience to Allah, you would not reach the dust of the sandal-strap of the mujahid in the path of Allah."" And a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed by which I may reach the deed of the mujahid in the path of Allah. He said: ""Even if you stood in prayer at night and fasted by day, you would not reach the sleep of the mujahid in the path of Allah."""
"3483","2306 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, saying: It reached me that Fadalah ibn Ubayd said: ""Islam is a spacious house; whoever enters it, it accommodates him. Emigration is a spacious house; whoever enters it, it accommodates him. And jihad is a spacious house; whoever enters it, it accommodates him. So whoever submits as a Muslim, emigrates, and strives has left no pursuit of good but sought it, and no escape from evil but fled through it."""
"3484","2307 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani narrated, from Amr ibn Malik, from one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When this verse was revealed, ""It was not proper for the people of Madinah and those around them of the bedouins to stay behind the Messenger of Allah,"" the whole verse, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him who sent me with the truth, were it not for the weak among the people, no expedition would go out without me being in it."""
"3485","2308 - Sa'id narrated: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated: al-Azhar ibn Abd Allah al-Harazi narrated: one who heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, while he was citing this verse, ""Then We caused to inherit the Book those We have chosen of Our servants; and among them is he who wrongs himself, and among them is he who is moderate, and among them is he who is foremost in good deeds"": ""Indeed our foremost are our people of jihad; indeed our moderate ones are our settled people; and indeed our wrongdoers are our bedouin people."" And Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, when he cited this verse, would say: ""Indeed our foremost one is foremost, our moderate one is saved, and our wrongdoer is forgiven."""
"3486","2309 - Sa'id narrated: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every community has a monasticism, and the monasticism of my community is jihad in the path of Allah."""
"3487","2310 - Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated: al-A'mash narrated, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a journey and said: ""There are men in Madinah: we never traveled a course nor crossed a valley but they were with us in it; sickness detained them."""
"3488","Chapter: Whoever leaves his house with nothing bringing him out but jihad. 2311 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, has guaranteed - or Allah has pledged, or Allah has undertaken - for whoever goes out as a mujahid in His path, with nothing bringing him out but jihad, faith in Allah and His Messenger, and belief in Him, that if He takes his life He will admit him to Paradise, or return him to the house he left, attaining whatever he attained of reward or booty."""
"3489","2312 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, has guaranteed for whoever strives in His path, with nothing bringing him out of his house but jihad in His path and belief in His word, that He will admit him to Paradise or return him to his dwelling with whatever he attained of reward or booty."""
"3490","2313 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: ""No raiding party raids in the path of Allah and gains booty but two-thirds of its reward is hastened to it out of its Hereafter reward; and if there is no booty, the reward is complete."""
"3491","Chapter: The excellence of the mujahids over those who sit back. 2314 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when tranquility came over him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell upon my thigh, and I never felt the weight of anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he was relieved of it, and he said to me: ""Write."" He said: So I wrote on a shoulder-blade, ""Not equal are those who sit back among the believers and the mujahids in the path of Allah,"" to the end of the verse. Then Ibn Umm Maktum, who was a blind man, when he heard the excellence of the mujahids, said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the believer who cannot perform jihad? When he finished speaking, tranquility came over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his thigh fell upon my thigh, and I felt of its weight the second time as I had felt the first time. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved of it, and he said: ""Read, O Zayd."" So I read, ""Not equal are those who sit back among the believers."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Except those with disability,"" the whole verse. Zayd said: Allah sent it down alone, and I attached it; and by Him in whose hand is my soul, it is as if I can still see where it was attached, at a crack in the shoulder-blade."
"3492","2315 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Hudayj ibn Sawmi, that Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to him that two men at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), partners in work - he says their work was almost equal - then one of them raided and the other sat back. So the one who sat back asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How much is the excellence of the mujahid in the path of Allah over the one who sits back? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One hundred degrees in Paradise."""
"3493","2316 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal: ""Those who strive for Allah are three, some better than others: a man who strives with his heart, loving for Allah and hating for Allah; a man who strives with his heart and his tongue, loving for Allah and hating for Allah, enjoining right and forbidding wrong, and fighting the polytheists alongside the Muslims - and this one is the best of them."""
"3494","2317 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, who said: The men of the conquest - Suhayl ibn Amr, al-Harith ibn Hisham, and Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza - came seeking permission from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he delayed admitting them. Al-Harith said: The people were called and you were called, but you lagged behind. When they entered upon Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, they said: O Commander of the Believers, what have we with you but what we see? He said: ""Yes, there is nothing but what you see."" They said: Then we seek what is higher than this. So they raided in the path of Allah until they died."
"3495","2318 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated: Umar ibn Ju'thum al-Yahsibi narrated to me, from Umarah ibn Khalid al-Maythami, that Abu Dharr used to say: Going out in the path of Allah was dearer to us than staying; and the hateful one among us was the one bloated with fat, with shining clothes - that is manliness among you today."
"3496","2319 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated: Musa ibn Ulayy narrated, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed the people at al-Jabiyah and said in his sermon: ""Whoever comes asking about the Qur'an, let him come to Ubayy ibn Ka'b; whoever comes asking about the lawful and the unlawful, let him come to Mu'adh ibn Jabal; whoever comes asking about inheritance shares, let him come to Zayd ibn Thabit; and whoever comes asking about wealth, let him come to me, for Allah has made me a treasurer. I shall begin with the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and give them, then with the Emigrants who were expelled from their homes and their wealth, then me and my companions, then with the Helpers who took the abode and faith before them. Then whoever hastened to emigration, the grant hastens to him; and whoever lagged behind emigration, the grant lags behind him. So let no man blame but the kneeling-place of his own mount."""
"3497","Chapter: What equals jihad in the path of Allah. 2320 - Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What equals jihad in the path of Allah? He said: ""You cannot do it."" He said: They repeated it to him twice or thrice, each time he said: ""You cannot do it."" And he said the third time: ""The parable of the mujahid in the path of Allah is like the parable of the fasting, standing, devout one with the verses of Allah, never flagging in fasting or prayer until the mujahid in the path of Allah returns."""
"3498","2321 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Hudayj ibn Sawmi al-Hajari, that he heard Akdar ibn Humam saying: A man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he said: We sat one day in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to a youth among us: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him what equals jihad. So he went to him and asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Nothing."" Then they sent him a second time and he said the like of it. Then we said: It is from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thrice; if he says ""Nothing,"" then say: What comes close to it? So he went to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Nothing."" He said: What comes close to it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Good speech, perpetual fasting, and Hajj every year; and nothing comes close to it after that."""
"3499","2322 - Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""The Muslims went out on the day of Badr with most of them on camels and walking on their feet."""
"3500","Chapter: Campaigning is of two kinds. 2323 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah and Bishr ibn Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-Sulami, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Azdi, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: ""Campaigning is of two kinds. As for the campaign in which the face of Allah is sought, in which the precious is spent, the deed is devoted, corruption is avoided, the partner is treated with ease, and the commander is obeyed - that one earns his sleep and his wakefulness until he returns. And as for the campaign in which the face of Allah is not sought - for show and repute, dissension and disobedience - that is the one who does not return even with bare sufficiency."""
"3501","2324 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from al-Harith ibn Yamjad al-Ash'ari, from Ibn Umar, who said: ""People in campaigning are two groups. One group went out remembering Allah much and reminding of Him, avoiding corruption on the march, consoling the companion, and spending the precious of their wealth - more delighted by what they spent than by what they gained of worldly things. When at the places of fighting, they were ashamed before Allah in those places that He should see doubt in their hearts or abandonment of the Muslims. When they could take from the spoils unlawfully, they purified their hearts and bodies of it, so Satan could neither tempt them nor speak to their hearts. Through them Allah strengthens His religion and suppresses His enemy. As for the other group, they went out without remembering Allah nor for His remembrance, without avoiding corruption, without consoling the companion, spending their wealth only unwillingly; what they spent of their wealth they saw as a fine, and Satan grieved them over it. When at the places of fighting, they were with the rearmost of the rearmost, the abandoning of the abandoning, clinging to mountain tops and hilltops. When the Muslims had a victory, they were the most eager in speaking falsehood; when they could take from the spoils unlawfully, they dared against Allah in it, and Satan told them it was booty. If ease befell them they exulted arrogantly, and if restraint befell them Satan tempted them with the Spoils. They have nothing of the reward of the Muslims except that their bodies are with their bodies and their march with their march, while their deeds and intentions are diverse - until Allah gathers them on the Day of Resurrection, then separates them."""
"3502","Chapter: Whoever equips a warrior or looks after him in his family. 2325 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has himself raided, and whoever looks after him in his family with good has himself raided."""
"3503","2326 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Yazid ibn Abi Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahri, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out to Banu Lihyan: ""Let one man of every two men go out."" Then he said to the one who sat back: ""Whichever of you looks after the one who went out in his family and wealth with good shall have half the reward of the one who went out."""
"3504","2327 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lives yet neither raids, nor equips a warrior, nor looks after him in his family with good, will not die until a calamity strikes him."""
"3505","2328 - Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Hajjaj, from Ata', from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever equips a pilgrim, or one performing umrah, or a warrior, or looks after him in his family, or breaks the fast of a fasting person, shall have the like of their rewards."""
"3506","2329 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever neither raids in the path of Allah, nor equips a warrior, nor looks after him in his family with good, will not die until a calamity strikes him."""
"3507","2330 - Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Habibah, who said: I was with Abu al-Darda' while I intended to raid, when a man came to him and said: My brother died and bequeathed a portion of his wealth to be given in charity, saying: Settle nothing until you come to Abu al-Darda'. In what do you think we should place it? He said: There is nothing in which it is placed better than the path of Allah. He said: I did not leave there but with a purse. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The parable of one who frees a slave at death is like the parable of one who gives a gift after satiety."""
"3508","Chapter: Whoever betrays a warrior in his family. 2331 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Qa'nab, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sanctity of the wives of the mujahids for those who sit back is like the sanctity of their mothers. There is no man among those who sit back who looks after a man among the mujahids in his family but he will be set up for him on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: This one looked after you in your family, so take of his good deeds whatever you wish. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: ""What do you think?"""
"3509","Chapter: Whoever raids while his parents are unwilling. 2332 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I set out for emigration, leaving my parents weeping. He said: ""Go and make them laugh as you made them weep."""
"3510","2333 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Shu'bah, from Ya'la ibn Ata', from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked his permission for jihad. He said to him: ""Is any father or mother alive?"" He said: My mother is alive. He said: ""Then go and honor her."" So he went off threading through the mounts, praising Allah."
"3511","2334 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to him, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a man emigrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have emigrated. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""You have abandoned polytheism, but it is jihad. Do you have anyone in Yemen?"" He said: My parents. He said: ""Did they permit you?"" He said: No. He said: ""Go back and ask their permission; if they permit you, then strive, otherwise honor them."""
"3512","2335 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Na'im, freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: A man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I pledge to you emigration and jihad, seeking reward from Allah. He said: ""Is any of your parents alive?"" He said: Yes, both of them. He said: ""Do you seek reward from Allah?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Return to your parents and keep good company with them."""
"3513","2336 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, that he asked Ubayd ibn Umayr: May a man raid while his parents, or one of them, are unwilling? He said: No."
"3514","2337 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abd Allah or Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, that Muhammad ibn Talhah wanted to raid, so his mother came to Umar and told him; Umar ordered him to obey his mother. Then he wanted again in the time of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, so his mother came to Uthman and told him; Uthman ordered him to stay. He said: Umar ordered me but did not compel me. He said: ""But I compel you."""
"3515","Chapter: The excellence of jihad, and that Hajj is the jihad of every weak one. 2338 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, who narrated to him from Awn ibn Abd Allah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, who said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard the people saying: Which deed is best, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Faith in Allah, jihad in His path, and an accepted Hajj."" Then he heard a call in the valley saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And I bear witness; no one bears witness to it but he is cleared of polytheism."""
"3516","2339 - Sa'id narrated: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated: Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq narrated, from A'ishah bint Talhah, from A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The jihad of women is Hajj."""
"3517","2340 - Sa'id narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr al-Hamdani narrated: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated, from Musa ibn Talhah, from A'ishah bint Talhah, from A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which deed is best? He said: ""Faith in Allah, jihad in the path of Allah, and an accepted Hajj."""
"3518","2341 - Sa'id narrated: Abu al-Ahwas narrated: Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq narrated, from A'ishah bint Talhah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which deed is best? He said: ""Faith in Allah, jihad in the path of Allah, and an accepted Hajj."""
"3519","2342 - Sa'id narrated: Salih ibn Musa narrated: Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq narrated, from Abayah ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij, from Ali ibn Husayn, who said: A man of the Helpers came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have obligated jihad upon myself, yet I am an old, sick elder with no strength in myself nor in my means. He said: ""Come to a jihad in which there is no thorn: Hajj."""
"3520","2343 - Sa'id narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr al-Hamdani narrated: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated, from Uthman ibn Sulayman, from his father's mother, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I want jihad in the path of Allah. He said: ""Shall I not guide you to a jihad in which there is no thorn?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Hajj to the House."""
"3521","2344 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said - if he did say it: ""The jihad of the old, the weak, and the woman is Hajj and umrah."""
"3522","Chapter: Campaigning after Hajj. 2345 - Sa'id narrated: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: It used to be said: ""A Hajj is better than a hundred campaigns, and a campaign is better than a hundred Hajjes."""
"3523","2346 - Sa'id narrated: Abu al-Ahwas narrated: Adam ibn Ali narrated, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: ""A campaign in the path of Allah is better than fifty Hajjes."""
"3524","2347 - Sa'id narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated, from his father, from Abu Kabshah al-Bara' ibn Qays al-Sakuni, who said: I was sitting with Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas while he was narrating to his companions, and he said at the end of his narration: ""O people, Allah has intended ease for you and has not intended hardship for you. By Allah, a campaign in the path of Allah is dearer to me than two Hajjes; a Hajj I make to the House of Allah is dearer to me than two umrahs; and an umrah I perform is dearer to me than three visits I make to Bayt al-Maqdis."""
"3525","2348 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, who said: Those seeking permission for Hajj from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were many on the day of the campaign of Tabuk, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A campaign for one who has already performed Hajj is better than forty Hajjes."""
"3526","Chapter: Alternating between Hajj and jihad. 2349 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: ""It is but a saddle and a camel-saddle: a saddle in the path of Allah, and a camel-saddle to the House of Allah."""
"3527","2350 - Sa'id narrated: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated: Mansur narrated, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabi'ah, from Umar, who said: I heard him one day addressing, saying: ""When you lay down the saddles, then bind the camel-saddles for Hajj or umrah; for it is one of the two jihads."""
"3528","2351 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ka'b, who said: ""The delegations to Allah are three: the pilgrim, the one performing umrah, and the warrior. Allah called them and they answered Him, and they asked Allah and He gave them."""
"3529","Chapter: Whoever said emigration has ceased. 2352 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, who said: It was said to Safwan - and that was after the Conquest - that there is no religion for one who does not emigrate. So he said: I shall not reach my dwelling until I come to Madinah. He lodged with al-Abbas and spent the night in the mosque, when a thief came and stole his striped cloak from under his head. He seized him and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered his hand cut. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is his. He said: ""Why not before you brought him to me? What brought you, O Abu Wahb?"" He said: It was said that there is no religion for one who has not emigrated. He said: ""Return, O Abu Wahb, to the valleys of Makkah; remain upon your dwellings, for emigration has ceased - but there is jihad and intention, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."""
"3530","2353 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi', from Ghaziyyah ibn al-Harith, that he informed him that youths of Quraysh wanted to emigrate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but their fathers prevented them. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no emigration after the Conquest; it is but the gathering, intention, and jihad."""
"3531","2354 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - some of them said: Emigration has ceased - disagreed about that, so we went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, people say emigration has ceased. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Emigration does not cease so long as there is jihad."""
"3532","Chapter: Sending the unmarried to raid in place of the married. 2355 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Mijlaz, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, ""used to send the unmarried to raid in place of the married."""
"3533","2356 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, that when booty came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would divide it the same day, giving the married two shares and the unmarried one share."
"3534","Chapter: A man given something to help him in the path of Allah. 2357 - Sa'id narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, who said: ""I wanted to raid, so I equipped myself with what I had. Then a man sent me aid of sixty dinars. I came to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and mentioned that to him, saying: Should I leave for my family the like of what I spent? He said: No; but when you reach the head of the campaign, it is like the rest of your wealth. Then I came to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and mentioned that to him, and he said the like of what Sa'id said."""
"3535","2358 - Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man given something in the path of Allah, who said: ""When he reaches the head of the campaign, it is like the rest of his wealth."""
"3536","2359 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that when he mounted someone on a camel in the path of Allah, he would say to him: ""If he headed for Syria: when you come to Wadi al-Qura on the road of Syria, then do with it as you do with your wealth; and if he headed for Egypt, he would say: When you come to Suqya on the road of Egypt, then do with it as you do with your wealth."""
"3537","2360 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Umar would accept what was given in the path of Allah and otherwise. Bakr said: And we never saw anyone deny that or change it. Bakr said: And Yasar informed me, from an elderly man of the Helpers, that a man met him and said: ""Are you a raider?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Take these five dinars and accept them."" Bakr said: And you do with what you were given in the path of Allah as you would do with your wealth."
"3538","Chapter: A man who raids for pay. 2361 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ma'dan ibn Hudayr al-Hadrami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The parable of those of my community who raid and take pay, strengthening themselves thereby against their enemy, is like the mother of Musa nursing her child and taking her wage."""
"3539","2362 - Sa'id narrated: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: A man came and said: O Mu'awiyah, a man raids and takes pay from his people - is that wholesome? He said: ""The parable of that is like the mother of Musa: she nursed her child and took her wage."""
"3540","2363 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr, that Ibn Munabbih - a man of Quraysh - sought a man to carry out his share for him and relieve him of his affair. When the hired man came to him, he said: I do not know what my share may amount to, and I would like you to name something for me whether there is a share or not. So he named three dinars for him. When the people gained booty, Ibn Munabbih wanted to divide his share for him along with the people. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the Prophet of Allah said: ""I find nothing for him in this campaign of his, in this world or the Hereafter, but the three dinars he took."""
"3541","2364 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Ali ibn Talhah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions, a man of the enemy came forth with a donkey before him bearing his load. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will duel this one?"" A man said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He went to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is the donkey and what is on it mine? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The donkey and what is on it are yours."" He went and dueled him, and the Muslim was killed. The people said: Praise be to Allah who granted him martyrdom. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""His is the donkey and what is on it."""
"3542","2365 - Sa'id narrated: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, who said: Alqamah asked Shurayh about pay for raiding. He said: He takes much and gives less than that, assigning it to the man - does that make you doubt? He said: Yes. He said: ""Then leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt."""
"3543","2366 - Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: He went out intending to hire himself for pay in an expedition that had set out against him; in the morning he was preparing, and I said to him: What is with you? Did you not intend to hire yourself? He said: ""Indeed, but last night I read Surah Bara'ah and heard it urging jihad."""
"3544","Chapter: Whoever said jihad continues. 2367 - Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Nushbah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things are of the root of faith: withholding from one who says there is no god but Allah - do not declare him an unbeliever for a sin, nor expel him from Islam for a deed; and jihad continues from when Allah sent me until the last of my community fights the Dajjal - neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just one annuls it; and faith in the decrees."""
"3545","2368 - Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated: Abu Raja' al-Jazari narrated, from al-Hasan, that he said: ""There will come upon people a time when they say: There is no jihad. When that happens, then strive, for jihad is best."""
"3546","2369 - Sa'id narrated: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Hisham, from al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sirin, who both said: ""Jihad against the polytheists stands."""
"3547","2370 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Umayr al-Suri, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah sent me with my sword before the Hour, made my provision under the shade of my spear, made humiliation and lowliness upon whoever opposes me, and whoever imitates a people is of them."""
"3548","2371 - Sa'id narrated: A man narrated - Da'laj said: I think it was Hushaym - who said: Mughirah informed us, saying: He was asked about raiding with the Banu Marwan, mentioning what they do, and he said: ""Nothing presents it but Satan, to hold them back from jihad against their enemy."" [Flag: isnad contains an unnamed man and uncertainty noted by Da'laj]"
"3549","2372 - Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma', from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There shall not cease to be a group of my community dominant upon the truth; those who abandon them shall not harm them, until the command of Allah comes, while they are so."""
"3550","2373 - Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated: Sayyar informed us, from Jubayr ibn Ubaydah - I think - from Abu Hurayrah, who said: ""This community shall not cease striving in the path of Allah, seeking the pleasure of Allah, victorious wherever they turn, cast into every cast; those who oppose them shall not harm them, until the command of Allah comes, while they are so."""
"3551","2374 - Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated: Sayyar informed us, from Jabr ibn Abidah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised us the campaign of India. If I reach it, I shall spend in it my wealth and myself; if I am killed in it, I am the best of martyrs, and if I return, I am Abu Hurayrah the freed."""
"3552","2375 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated: Shu'bah narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There shall not cease to be people of my community victorious; those who abandon them shall not harm them, until the Hour comes."""
"3553","2376 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There shall not cease to be a band of my community dominant upon the truth, not caring who opposes them, until the False Messiah, the Dajjal, comes out and they fight him."""
"3554","2377 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, saying: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Ata' ibn Yazid, who said: ""I heard Abu Ayyub in the campaign of Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah."" [Flag: matn appears truncated in source, ending abruptly]"
"3555","Chapter: The excellence of a morning or evening expedition in the path of Allah. 2378 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman al-Mu'addib narrated, saying: I heard Abu Hazim mentioning from Sahl ibn Sa'd, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Flag: matn appears truncated in source]"
"3556","2379 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition among whom was Mu'adh ibn Jabal. The people went in the morning and Mu'adh ibn Jabal stayed behind until he prayed noon with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, and said: ""Do I not see the people have preceded you by a month in Paradise? Join your companions."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I wanted to pray with you and have you supplicate for me, that I might thereby have excellence over my companions. He said: ""Rather they have excellence over you. Join your companions."" And he said: ""An evening journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and a morning journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."""
"3557","Chapter: The day in which going out is recommended, and at what time to go out. 2380 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never went out on a journey but on Thursday."""
"3558","2381 - Sa'id narrated: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ""when he traveled, liked to travel on Thursday at the beginning of the day."""
"3559","2382 - Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated: Ya'la ibn Ata' informed us: Umarah ibn Hadid narrated, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, bless my community in its early mornings."" When he sent an expedition he would send them at the beginning of the day. Sakhr was a merchant, and he would send his traders at the beginning of the day, so he became rich and his wealth multiplied."
"3560","Chapter: What armies are commanded when they go out. 2383 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Ubaydah, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, when he appointed over the troops - Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan over a troop, Amr ibn al-As over a troop, Shurahbil ibn Hasanah over a troop, and appointed Khalid ibn al-Walid over a troop, then made Yazid over the whole force - went out with him to bid him farewell and instruct him, while Yazid was riding and Abu Bakr walked beside him. Yazid said: O Successor of the Messenger of Allah, either you ride or I dismount and walk with you. He said: I shall neither ride nor let you dismount; I reckon this step in the path of Allah. O Yazid, you will come to a land where varieties of foods will be brought to you; mention Allah's name when you eat and praise Him when you finish. O Yazid, you will meet people who have shaved the middle of their heads so they are like headbands; split their skulls with swords. You will pass by people in hermitages of theirs who have confined themselves therein; leave them until Allah kills them therein upon their error. O Yazid, do not kill a child, nor a woman, nor a small one; do not destroy an inhabited place, do not hamstring a fruit-bearing tree, nor a mute beast, nor a cow, nor a sheep except for food; do not burn a palm nor drown it; do not steal from the spoils, and do not be cowardly."
"3561","2384 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, freedman of Abd al-Rahman, that he said: A man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked permission to raid, and he permitted him, saying: ""If you meet, do not be cowardly; if you gain power, do not steal from the spoils; do not burn a palm nor hamstring it; do not cut a fruit-bearing tree; do not kill a beast in which you have no need; and beware harming the believer."""
"3562","2385 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahiq, from Ibn Isam al-Muzani, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition and said: ""When you see a mosque or hear a caller to prayer, do not kill anyone."""
"3563","2386 - Sa'id narrated: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Salt and Abu al-Musafi', who both said: Umar wrote to us while we were at Nahawand: ""Establish prayer at its time; when you meet, do not flee; and when you gain booty, do not steal from it."""
"3564","Chapter: The best armies, the best expeditions, and the best companions. 2387 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Haywah, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of companions are four, the best of expeditions four hundred, and the best of armies four thousand."""
"3565","2388 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Haywah, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of companions with Allah is the best of them to his companion, and the best of neighbors is the best of them to his neighbor."""
"3566","Chapter: Sailing the sea. 2389 - Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, spoke to this western sea, saying: 'O sea, I created you, perfected your creation, and multiplied water in you; and I shall carry in you servants of Mine who magnify Me, praise Me, glorify Me, and declare My oneness. How will you treat them?' It said: I shall drown them. He said: Your might is in your edges, and I shall carry them upon My hand.' And Allah spoke to the eastern sea, saying: 'O sea, I created you, perfected your creation, and multiplied water in you; and I shall carry in you servants of Mine who magnify Me, praise Me, glorify Me, and declare My oneness. How will you treat them?' It said: Then I shall glorify You with them, declare Your oneness with them, and carry them between my back and my belly. So its Lord rewarded it with ornament and game."""
"3567","2390 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, that al-Ala' ibn Isma'il narrated to him that it was mentioned to him that when Allah created the sea, He said: ""How when I carry upon you a creation of My creation?"" It said: I shall not settle them upon my back. He said: ""Rather - your might shall be in your edges; I shall make your might in your edges."" [Flag: source wording garbled at this point; translated literally]"
"3568","2391 - Sa'id narrated: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated, from Zuhayr ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps on a rooftop with no structure around him to hold back his feet, and perishes, is absolved of protection; and whoever sails the sea when it is agitated is absolved of protection."""
"3569","2392 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, who said: ""None shall sail the sea but a pilgrim, one performing umrah, or a warrior in the path of Allah."""
"3570","2393 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Mutarrif, from Bishr Abu Abd Allah, from Bashir ibn Muslim, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None shall sail the sea but a pilgrim, one performing umrah, or a warrior in the path of Allah; for beneath the sea is fire, and beneath the fire is sea. And do not ever buy anything from one under the pressure of authority."""
"3571","2394 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar al-Bahrani, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to the people: ""As for the sea, we see its way is like the way of the land. Allah has subjected the sea to you that ships may run in it by His command and that you may seek of His bounty. So we permit sailing the sea for trade to whoever wishes; none of the people shall be barred from it."""
"3572","Chapter: The excellence of the sea and the martyr in it. 2395 - Sa'id narrated: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: ""A campaign at sea equals ten on land, and the seasick one at sea is like one wallowing in his blood on land."""
"3573","2396 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Shu'bah, from Ya'la ibn Ata', from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: ""That I raid at sea is dearer to me than to spend an accepted qintar in the path of Allah."""
"3574","2397 - Sa'id narrated: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Ifriqi narrated, from Abu Yasar al-Sulami, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: ""What a fine campaign is the sea - were it not for one thing: were it not that the servant, closest as he is to martyrdom, calls upon Allah to deliver him from it."""
"3575","2398 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr informed me, that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, that Ka'b al-Ahbar used to say: ""For the man of the sea over the man of the land is of excellence: that when he sets his foot in it, if he is devoted, the gates of Paradise are opened for him. If he is killed or drowned, he shall have like the reward of two martyrs; reward is written for him from when he boards it until he sails, like the reward of a man whose neck was struck in the path of Allah while he wallows in his blood. A day at sea is better than a month on land, and a month at sea is better than a year on land."""
"3576","2399 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Amr ibn Muhajir, from his father, from Tubay', from Ka'b al-Ahbar, who said: ""When a man sets his foot in the ship, he leaves his sins behind his back, like the day his mother bore him. The seasick one in it is like one wallowing in his blood in the path of Allah, and the patient one in it is like a king with a crown on his head."""
"3577","2400 - Sa'id narrated: Abu al-Harish al-Qassar narrated: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from a man, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: Had I been a man, I would not have striven but at sea; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever is struck by seasickness at sea is like one wallowing in his blood on land."""
"3578","Chapter: Whose feet become dusty in the path of Allah. 2401 - Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Safwan ibn Abi Yazid, from al-Qa'qa' ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell shall not gather in the belly of a servant, nor shall miserliness and faith ever gather in the belly of a servant."""
"3579","2402 - Sa'id narrated: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Safwan ibn Abi Yazid, from Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Miserliness and faith shall not gather in the belly of a Muslim man, nor shall dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell gather in the belly of a Muslim man."""
"3580","Chapter: Spending in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic. 2403 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, who said: When the delegation of the people of Syria came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, he asked them, saying: ""How do you reckon your spendings?"" They said: At seven hundred. He said: ""Do so; and when one of you reaches his family, let him reckon a male child - rightly or wrongly - Allah gave him or withheld from him."" [Flag: closing clause obscure in source; translated literally]"
"3581","2404 - Sa'id narrated - and Abu Mu'awiyah - from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, concerning His saying, ""And do not cast yourselves with your own hands into destruction"": he said: ""Abandoning spending."""
"3582","2405 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih or another, from Mujahid, concerning His saying, ""And do not cast yourselves with your own hands into destruction"": he said: ""Let not fear of poverty prevent you from spending in the path of Allah."""
"3583","Chapter: Service, and the stud-fee of the horse. 2406 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Damrah ibn Habib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The greatest of people in reward is their servant."""
"3584","2407 - Sa'id narrated: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: ""A man's service, when his servant serves his companions in the path of Allah."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best after that? He said: ""A structure a man builds over his companions in the path of Allah."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best after that? He said: ""The stud-service of a horse whose owner carries him upon it in the path of Allah."""
"3585","2408 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Sulayman ibn Umar, that it reached him that it used to be said: ""Three - none knows what reward is in them: the man of service in the path of Allah, the man of shade in the path of Allah, and the man of the horse's stud-service."""
"3586","Chapter: The excellence of ribat. 2409 - Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir saying: Salman passed by Ibn al-Simt while he was stationed with his companions, and it had become hard upon them. Salman said to him: O Ibn al-Simt, shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I heard him say: ""Ribat of a day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month and standing it in prayer; whoever dies in it is protected from the trial of the grave, and his deed grows for him until the Day of Resurrection."""
"3587","2410 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated: Ata' al-Khurasani narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: ""Ribat of a day in the path of Allah is dearer to me than coinciding with the Night of Decree in one of the two mosques: the Sacred Mosque and the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whoever keeps ribat three days in the path of Allah has kept ribat; and whoever keeps ribat forty days has completed ribat."""
"3588","2411 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Umamah, who said: ""Every deed of the son of Adam ceases when its doer dies, except ribat; it continues for its doer like the reward of the living one keeping ribat, until the Day of Resurrection."""
"3589","2412 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ismah ibn Rashid, who said: I heard men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preferring ribat over jihad. I said to my father: Why? He said: ""Because in jihad there are many conditions, and there are none in ribat."""
"3590","2413 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ishaq al-Azraq, that Abu Salim al-Jayshani narrated to him that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: ""Every deed ceases for its doer when he dies, except the one keeping ribat; ribat continues for him until he is raised from his grave."""
"3591","2414 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abu Hani' informed me, from Amr ibn Malik, from Fadalah ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every dead one has his deed sealed, except the one keeping ribat in the path of Allah; his deed grows for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is secured from the tormentor of the grave."""
"3592","2415 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ata' al-Khurasani, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the people of the graveyard,"" three times. He was asked about that, and he said: That is a graveyard that shall be at Asqalan. So Ata' used to keep ribat there forty days every year until he died."
"3593","Chapter: Whoever keeps guard in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic. 2416 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated: Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah informed, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the guard of guards."""
"3594","2417 - Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz, from his father, who said: ""Whoever keeps guard in the path of Allah, Allah writes for him for every night a qirat of reward, equal to the number of those he left behind him, Muslim or unbeliever."""
"3595","Chapter: Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah. 2418 - Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid plucking white hair."
"3596","2419 - Sa'id narrated: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated: Luqman ibn Amir narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, from Amr ibn Abasah, who said: I said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no disparagement in it nor error. He said: I heard him say: ""Whoever has three children born to him in Islam and they are taken before reaching puberty, Allah admits him to Paradise by His abounding mercy to them; whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah that reaches the enemy - hit or miss - it equals freeing a slave; whoever frees a believing slave, Allah frees, for every limb of it, a limb of him from the Fire; and whoever spends two pairs in the path of Allah - Paradise has eight gates, and he enters through whichever of them he wishes."""
"3597","2420 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sulayman ibn Abd Allah or Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, freedman of Abd al-Rahman, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, who said to Amr ibn Abasah: O Amr, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no addition nor omission. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever grows a white hair in Islam, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever shoots the enemy with an arrow and his arrow reaches - miss or hit - it equals a slave; and whoever frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire, every limb for a limb."""
"3598","2421 - Sa'id narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated, from Abu Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: ""Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it shall be light for him; whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah that reaches the enemy, a good deed is written for him thereby and a sin removed from him; whoever frees a Muslim person, it shall be his ransom from the Fire, for every two limbs of the two a limb of him; whoever reads five hundred verses is written among the devout; and whoever reads a thousand verses, a qintar is written for him."" It was said: How much is the qintar? He said: A thousand and two hundred ounces; and the qintar is better than the world and what is in it, or what is between heaven and earth."
"3599","Chapter: Whoever fasts in the path of Allah, or his head is split. 2422 - Sa'id narrated: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi narrated, saying: I heard Sa'id al-Maqburi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""No man fasts a day in the path of Allah but Allah removes him from the Fire by seventy autumns."""
"3600","2423 - Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns."""
